      "narrative": "Ursa Space Systems is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised approximately $67M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 7 private-sector peers in the same stage and adjacent stages (Series B through D), including Sierra Space, Impulse Space, Apex Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, and Varda Space Industries, alongside 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($67M) as a proxy for early-stage value and applying a typical Series C-to-next-stage multiplier of 1.7x, implies a valuation of $114M. Peer-median analysis across the 7 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring using the sector P/S median of 24.6x cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure for Ursa.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $97M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median estimate of $1.1B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage positioning and revenue traction relative to peers. The peer-median method carries greater weight given the robust sample size; however, without visibility into Ursa's revenue and unit economics relative to comparables, the lower stage-progression estimate cannot be dismissed and likely represents downside risk if the company's commercial progress lags peer expectations.",
