      "narrative": "AheadComputing is a Seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Debbie Marr, Mark Dechene, Jonathan Pearce, and Srikanth Srinivasan. The company has raised $51.5M to date. The relevant comp universe includes 3 public semiconductor players (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers, including Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched.\n\nOf three valuation methods evaluated, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($51.5M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A progression yields an implied valuation of $129M. The Peer-Median method could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or tightly-filtered peers in the semiconductor space; while 13 same-sector companies exist in the comp set, fewer than 3 meet narrow stage and valuation-tier criteria. Public-Comp Anchoring was not applicable given the absence of disclosed revenue data, though the median public semiconductor P/S multiple stands at 20.4x.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $109M (low) to $148M (high), centered at $129M. This range reflects significant uncertainty: the reliance on a single method and the absence of meaningful peer-stage data limit conviction. The lack of revenue disclosure prevents cross-check via revenue multiples. Key uncertainties include burn rate, product maturity, and IP defensibility relative to the identified private peer set.",
