      "narrative": "CubeFabs is a Series E-stage semiconductor company founded by Matthew Putman (PhD, CEO; former Columbia materials science professor) and John Putman. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 11 comparable companies: 3 public peers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private-stage competitors including SambaNova Systems, Etched, Ayar Labs, Tenstorrent, and Nearfield Instruments.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the company's $182M total capital raised as a proxy, applying a 1.4x step-up multiplier typical of Series E advancement, yielding $255M. Peer-median analysis identifies 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $3.8B (range: $1.6B\u2013$11.0B). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures, standard for private companies.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $217M (low) to $4.3B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty around CubeFabs' relative positioning within the frontier-chip sector: whether the company aligns more closely with earlier-stage peers near $1.6B\u2013$2.7B or with later-stage, higher-valued entrants at $5.0B\u2013$11.0B. Revenue trajectory and product-market validation remain key determinants not visible in this quantitative framework.",
