      "narrative": "Aurora Innovation, a public-stage autonomous systems company founded by Urmson, Anderson, and Bagnell, has raised $2.0B to date. The Drones & Autonomous sector contains seven same-sector peers, of which eight are private companies including Joby Aviation, Archer Aviation, Waymo, Wayve, and Zipline. No direct public comparables exist in this narrow space.\n\nPeer-median valuation analysis is not applicable here. The identified peer set lacks sufficient depth: only two same-stage comparables were identified, zero adjacent-stage peers, and zero similar-valuation-tier matches\u2014all falling short of the minimum three-datapoint threshold required for reliable triangulation. Relying on all-sector median data would introduce material distortion given the heterogeneity of business models and maturity levels within Drones & Autonomous.\n\nThe scarcity of comparable public benchmarks and the thinness of private peer data at Aurora's scale create significant analytical constraints. A defensible valuation range cannot be supported by the available quantitative evidence. Valuation work on this target would require alternative methods\u2014such as DCF sensitivity analysis tied to autonomous vehicle adoption timelines, or transaction-based precedent from the eight private peers\u2014alongside explicit documentation of model assumptions regarding regulatory approval, commercialization runway, and capital intensity. The primary uncertainty remains the absence of meaningful public market pricing for this business model.",
