      "narrative": "SendCutSend is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised approximately $110M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable, all operating in the robotics and manufacturing sector at Series A through Series B stages. Key peers include Humanoid ($1.4B, Series A), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression approach applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $110M total raised as a proxy base, yielding $220M. The peer-median method references five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.6B and a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. These peers span Series B (Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity), Series A (Humanoid), and Seed (Walden Robotics) stages.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $187M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $935M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around whether SendCutSend's traction and market position align with earlier-stage peers near $220M or more mature Series B benchmarks approaching $1.6B\u2013$2.0B. Key variables include customer concentration, unit economics, and pathway to Series B deployment.",
