      "narrative": "Plantd Materials is a Series B\u2013stage housing and construction company founded by Nathan Silvernail, Huade Tan, and Josh Dorfman. The company has raised $42M to date. The comparable universe consists of four private peers in the same sector: Cuby Technologies, Cover, Somos, and Charge Robotics. No public housing/construction comps were available for direct benchmarking.\n\nStage-progression analysis was the applicable valuation method. Using total capital raised of $42M as a proxy for current embedded value, a typical Series B\u2013to\u2013next\u2013stage step-up multiplier of 1.9x yields an implied valuation of $80M. This methodology reflects the expectation that capital deployment and operational milestones justify meaningful expansion of enterprise value between Series B and subsequent funding rounds.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $68M (low) to $92M (median $80M), centered on the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the absence of public market comparables, which limits ability to anchor valuations to traded multiples of revenue, EBITDA, or other normalized metrics. The single-method triangulation reflects limited data availability; additional color on the private peer set's revenue scales, unit economics, and recent valuations would strengthen conviction in the range and potentially reveal whether Plantd commands premium or discount positioning within its peer cohort.",
