      "narrative": "Critical Energy, founded by Spencer Jackson, is a seed-stage climate and energy company that has raised $22M to date. The comparable universe in Climate & Energy comprises one public company (LNZA) and eight private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables\u2014zero companies met the narrow filtering criteria of stage proximity and valuation tier\u2014rendering traditional peer-median analysis inapplicable.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable lens. Using total capital raised ($22M) as a value proxy and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the subsequent round yields an implied valuation of $55M. This method assumes the company's capital efficiency and market conditions track sector norms for early-stage progression.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $47M to $63M, centered on $55M. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct peer benchmarks at Critical Energy's stage, limiting calibration of the stage-progression multiple; the nascent state of the frontier climate-tech sector, where step-up multiples may diverge materially from historical norms; and incomplete visibility into the company's unit economics, burn rate, and technical milestones. Additional comparable data or revised stage assumptions would materially sharpen this estimate.",
