      "narrative": "Farcast is a Series A space & aerospace company founded by Siamak Ebadi that has raised $23.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set spanning five public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and eight private comparables including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, representing the addressable frontier-tech landscape in the sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable given available data. Stage-progression anchors to the $23.6M total raised as a proxy for current post-money value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage transitions, yielding $47M. Peer-median analysis uses three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Starcloud at $1.1B), producing a $1.3B median with a $1.1B\u2013$2.0B range. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 24.6x across six tickers) cannot be applied absent Farcast's revenue disclosure.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $40M to $1.5B, with a median of $674M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty: the stage-progression method yields conservative floor estimates, while peer medians\u2014drawn from more mature, later-stage competitors\u2014likely overstate near-term value. Key dependencies include Farcast's revenue trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peers, and the specific nature of competitive positioning within the satellite/launch services spectrum. Revenue visibility and detailed unit economics would narrow this range substantially.",
