      "narrative": "Phaidra is a Series B AI & Software company led by former DeepMind engineers (including AlphaGo core contributor Vedavyas Panneershelvam) and ex-Google industrial AI program lead Jim Gao. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (Palantir), with primary focus on 3 same-stage AI & Software peers: Physical Intelligence ($5.6B), Black Forest Labs ($3.2B), and Field AI ($2.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, anchoring to Phaidra's $120M total raised, applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying $228M. The peer-median method uses the $3.2B median across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables, with a range spanning $2.0B to $5.6B. This significant dispersion reflects heterogeneity within AI infrastructure and applied AI verticals.\n\nTriangulating these approaches yields a median valuation of $1.7B, with a low bound of $194M and a high bound of $3.7B. The wide range reflects two competing signals: the stage-progression method suggests conservatism relative to peer valuations, while the peer-median reflects market exuberance for frontier AI talent. Key uncertainties include Phaidra's revenue, unit economics, and whether industrial-AI-specific expertise commands the valuation premium observed in the peer set.",
