      "narrative": "Spaceium is a seed-stage space & aerospace company founded by Ashi Dissanayake and Reza Fetanat, both from University of Ottawa with deep domain expertise in orbital mechanics, propulsion, and legacy engine systems. The company has raised $6.3M to date. The broader Space & Aerospace sector includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 identifiable private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nA single valuation method was reliably applicable to this profile. The Stage-Progression approach uses the $6.3M total raised as a proxy for current enterprise value, then applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A advancement in this sector, yielding $15.75M. This method is grounded in observable venture capital deployment patterns rather than speculative revenue assumptions. Public comparables exist\u2014the Space & Aerospace median trades at 24.6x revenue\u2014but Spaceium's private revenue remains undisclosed, precluding P/S anchoring. Private peer benchmarking was also inapplicable due to an insufficient narrow peer set at the same stage and valuation tier.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $13M to $18M, centered on $16M. The primary uncertainty is the absence of revenue or near-term commercial traction data; valuation is anchored entirely to capital efficiency at seed stage rather than forward business metrics. Material upside or downside will depend on achieving technical milestones and revenue demonstration before the next capital round.",
