      "narrative": "Blackstar is a Seed-stage AI & Software company founded by Daniel Edrisian, former OpenAI Codex engineer whose prior venture (Alex, YC W24) was acqui-hired by OpenAI in September 2025. The company has raised $12M to date. The broader AI & Software sector includes 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (Palantir), though a sufficiently narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier was not available for robust median-based triangulation.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression analysis was the primary applicable method. Using total raised ($12M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical Seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $30M. A peer-median approach was not feasible; the broader AI & Software sector contained 12 peers, but filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier comparables yielded fewer than three datapoints, making median benchmarking unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $26M to $34M, with a median point of $30M. This range reflects the stage-progression method applied conservatively (low-end) and with upside sensitivity (high-end). Key uncertainties include the absence of direct, same-stage peer data for cross-validation and reliance on a single methodological input. The founder's prior exit to OpenAI and EECS pedigree provide credential support, though near-term revenue or product traction data were not provided for revenue-based validation.",
