      "narrative": "PAVE Space is a Seed-stage space & aerospace company founded by Julie B\u00f6hning and J\u00e9r\u00e9m\u00e9 Marciacq, both co-founders of Gruy\u00e8re Space Program at EPFL. The company has raised $40M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public Space & Aerospace players (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Starcloud, SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method, applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed to next-stage advancement. Using $40M total raised as a valuation proxy yields an implied valuation of $100M. Peer-median analysis could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage private comparables (only 1 narrow-filter match identified across 14 same-sector peers). Public comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median: 24.6x across 6 tickers) cannot be executed without target revenue disclosure, which is unavailable for private companies.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $85M to $115M, with $100M as the median estimate. This range rests narrowly on one method and assumes standard stage-transition multiples hold for PAVE's profile. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue metrics, insufficient private peer data for cross-validation, and unknown product maturity relative to public comparables. Further diligence on commercialization timeline and technical differentiation is warranted before final valuation.",
