      "narrative": "Epirus is a Series D-stage defense and security company that has raised $550M+ to date. Valuation analysis relies on a peer universe of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms operating in the same sector. The five most recent private comparables span a valuation range of $2.1B to $9.2B.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the company's last post-money valuation of $1.4B, yielding $2.0B. Peer-median analysis of five same-stage, same-sector private companies produces a median valuation of $4.5B, with a range between $2.1B (True Anomaly, Onebrief) and $9.2B (Saronic). Triangulating these two methods produces a low-to-high range of $1.7B to $5.2B, with a midpoint of $3.3B.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.7B to $5.2B, with a median estimate of $3.3B. Key uncertainties include the dispersion within the peer set\u2014the $9.2B valuation for Saronic represents material upside optionality but also suggests heterogeneous risk profiles across comparables. The stage-progression method, which anchors to the last fundraise, may understate current value if operating metrics or market conditions have improved materially since that round.",
