      "narrative": "Saronic, a Series D defense and security company founded by Mavrookas, Lehman, Altekar, and Lambert, has raised $2.6B+ to date against a current post-money valuation of $9.25B. The peer universe comprises 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014operating in the same sector and stage cohort, including Quantum-Systems, Chaos Industries, True Anomaly, Onebrief, and Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate defensibly to Saronic's fair value. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 1.5x typical Series D step-up multiplier to the prior $4.0B post-money round, implies $6.0B. Peer-median benchmarking across the 4-company same-sector, same-stage sample (Quantum-Systems at $8.0B, Chaos Industries at $4.5B, True Anomaly at $2.2B, Onebrief at $2.1B) yields a median valuation of $3.4B, with a range spanning $2.1B to $8.0B.\n\nSynthesis of both methods produces a triangulated valuation band of $2.8B (low) to $6.9B (high), with a median of $4.7B. The current $9.25B valuation sits substantially above the high end of this range, reflecting either differentiated operational performance or market timing assumptions not captured in peer comparables. Key uncertainties include revenue traction relative to the peer set, capital intensity through exit, and the composition of future Series E/F participation.",
