      "narrative": "Castelion is a Series C defense and security company founded by Bryon Hargis, Sean Pitt, and Andrew Kreitz, currently valued at $13.0B post-money after raising $1.25B+ in equity across three rounds ($100M Series A, $350M Series B, $800M Series C) plus a $250M credit facility. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 15 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies, including 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers such as Stark Defence, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $1.0B last post-money valuation and a typical Series C-to-next-stage multiplier of 1.7x, implies $1.7B. Peer-median analysis across the 15-company Defense & Security comp set yields a median valuation of $2.2B, with a range spanning $300M to $9.2B; relevant private peers in the dataset include Stark Defence at $4.0B (Series C) and Chaos Industries at $4.5B (Series D).\n\nTriangulation across these two methods supports a fair-value range of $1.4B to $2.5B, with a median estimate of $1.9B. The current $13.0B valuation sits substantially above both methods and the peer-median benchmark, creating material downside risk. Key uncertainties include revenue growth trajectory, customer concentration in the defense sector, and execution risk in scaling operations post-Series C.",
