      "narrative": "Reflect Orbital is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Ben Nowack and Tristan Semmelhack that has raised $35.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, with a focused peer set of 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $35M raised proxy, implying a $70M valuation. The peer-median method examines three comparables (Cowboy Space at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Starcloud at $1.1B Seed), yielding a median implied value of $1.3B and a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales (median 24.6x across the sector) cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue data.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $60M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median point of $685M. The wide spread reflects material methodological divergence: stage-progression conservatively weights recent capital deployment, while peer-median is anchored to later-stage comparables with significant valuation inflation. Key uncertainties include the target's current revenue run-rate, time to Series B funding, and whether early-stage space infrastructure commands sector multiples or discounts relative to more mature peers.",
