      "narrative": "Firefly Aerospace is a publicly traded Space & Aerospace company founded by Tom Markusic, currently valued at approximately $2.9B following an $868M IPO. The valuation analysis draws from a comparables universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage public peers: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across these 4 public space companies stands at $23.8B, with a wide dispersion reflecting the sector's heterogeneity\u2014ranging from $840M (Astroscale) to $1.6T (SpaceX). Public-Comp Anchoring using Price-to-Sales multiples is not applicable, as Firefly's revenue is not on file; while the broader Space & Aerospace sector (6 public tickers) trades at a median 24.6x P/S, this multiple cannot be meaningfully applied without disclosed revenue.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range derived from available methods is $20.2B (low) to $27.3B (high), with a median of $23.8B. This implies significant upside from Firefly's current $2.9B valuation. However, this analysis carries material uncertainty: reliance on a single applicable method, extreme comparables dispersion (a 1,900x range from Astroscale to SpaceX), and the lack of revenue-based anchoring limit conviction. The wide peer spread reflects fundamentally different business models and market positions within aerospace, making direct median application subject to substantial judgment regarding which peers most resemble Firefly's specific mission and stage.",
