      "narrative": "Formic is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Saman Farid and Misa Ilkhechi, having raised $56M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies alongside 1 public comparable, supplemented by a broader universe of 8 private peers including Humanoid, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchored to the $56M total raised as a proxy for current post-money valuation, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, yielding $112M. Peer-median analysis references five robotics companies at Series B, Series A, and Seed stages with valuations ranging from $1.1B to $2.0B; the median across this set is $1.6B. The two methods produce materially different signals, reflecting stage and company-maturity dispersion within the peer universe.\n\nTriangulation across these two approaches implies a valuation range of $95M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $881M. The wide range reflects genuine uncertainty around whether Formic's trajectory aligns with earlier-stage, lower-valuation comparables or with more mature Series B peers commanding billion-dollar multiples. Key uncertainties include product-market fit validation, revenue traction relative to peers, and capital efficiency. A narrower range would require additional revenue and growth-rate data.",
