      "narrative": "New Limit is a Series C-stage biotech & health company founded by Brian Armstrong, Blake Byers, and Jacob Kimmel, having raised $610M+ to date at a current post-money valuation of $3.1B. The peer universe consists of 11 comparable companies: 8 private and 3 public (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L), selected for sector alignment and similar valuation tier.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C-to-later-stage transitions, implying a valuation of $5.3B based on the $3.1B last post-money. Peer-median analysis across five comparable companies\u2014Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), Recursion Pharmaceuticals ($1.6B), Freenome ($1.1B), and Alto Neuroscience ($1.0B)\u2014yields a median of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring using sector P/S multiples cannot be applied due to lack of disclosed revenue data for the target.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $1.4B (low) to $6.1B (high), with a median of $3.4B. The wide range reflects substantial dispersion in peer outcomes within the biotech sector. Key uncertainties include the stage-progression multiplier's relevance given heterogeneous investor appetite in frontier biotech, the appropriate peer selection across diverse therapeutic modalities, and undisclosed revenue or near-term clinical milestones that could materially alter comparable valuations.",
