      "narrative": "Nucleus Genomics is a Series A-stage biotech company led by founder Kian Sadeghi that has raised $32M to date. The valuation exercise draws on a comparable universe of 3 public peers in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. This method uses total capital raised ($32M) as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage step-ups, yielding $64M. Peer-median anchoring was not viable: while 7 same-sector peers exist, none of the narrower filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar-tier) produced the minimum 3 datapoints needed for statistical confidence. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied because Nucleus Genomics does not disclose revenue, a requirement for price-to-sales multiples. The median public Biotech & Health P/S ratio is 7.4x across the three tickers, but remains unusable without target revenue.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $54M to $74M, with a median point estimate of $64M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable financials from the private peer set, undisclosed revenue trajectory, and clinical or regulatory milestones that could materially alter risk profile between now and Series B.",
