      "narrative": "Xcimer Energy is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Conner Galloway and Alexander Valys, having raised over $100M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 11 peers\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private-stage firms including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy\u2014spanning seed through Series B stages within nuclear energy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods anchor this analysis. Stage-progression methodology applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier from the $100M total raised proxy, implying a $200M valuation consistent with next-stage advancement. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Valar Atomics at $6.0B Series B, Nano Nuclear Energy at $808M Seed, Fuse Energy at $200M Series A) yields a median valuation of $808M, with observed range of $200M\u2013$6.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $170M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $504M. The wide dispersion\u2014driven primarily by the outlier Valar Atomics valuation at the upper end\u2014reflects material stage and maturity differences within the peer set. Key uncertainties include capital intensity and timeline to commercialization, typical of frontier nuclear technologies. The $200M\u2013$808M band represents the most defensible range given stage-appropriate peer anchors and step-up progression logic.",
