      "narrative": "Base Power, a Series C climate and energy company founded by Zach Dell and Justin Lopas, has raised over $1.0B to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), supplemented by a broader comparable universe of 8 private frontier-tech players and 1 public benchmark (LNZA).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method applied a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $1.0B total-raised proxy, yielding $1.7B. The peer-median method across the three same-stage, same-sector comparables produced $1.0B, with an observed range of $700M to $3.0B. These approaches do not converge tightly, reflecting high dispersion in early-stage climate-tech valuations.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $850M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.4B. The substantial width of this range reflects uncertainty around both Base Power's relative technical progress versus named peers and the maturity of comparable company financials. The peer-median sits at the lower bound of the range, while stage-progression suggests moderate step-up room. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to peers and time-to-inflection for the underlying technology.",
