      "narrative": "Auterion, a Series B defense and security company, is evaluated against a peer universe of 8 private and 2 public comparables in the same sector and stage. The private peer set spans valuations from $300M to $3.0B, with Dream Security, Allen Control Systems, and Harmattan AI representing the upper quartile at $3.0B, $2.2B, and $1.4B respectively.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, anchoring to $130M in total raised and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implied a value of $247M. The peer-median method, based on 8 same-stage, same-sector private comparables, yielded a median valuation of $1.1B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B. This significant methodological divergence reflects dispersion within the Defense & Security peer set and uncertainty regarding Auterion's relative positioning within that cohort.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $210M (low) to $1.3B (high), with a median of $686M. The wide dispersion\u2014spanning over 6x from low to high\u2014underscores material uncertainty around revenue scale, customer concentration, and defensibility relative to the peer set. Resolution of these factors, particularly evidence of traction relative to the upper-quartile peers cited, would be necessary to narrow the range materially.",
