      "narrative": "Deterrence is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $10M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 peers spanning public equities (2 companies: DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and private venture-backed firms (8 companies including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI), representing the same sector and adjacent funding stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $10M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage transitions, yielding $25M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B Seed stage; Singularity at $400M Series A; NODA AI at $125M Series A), producing a median valuation of $400M with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $21M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $212M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around which peer cohort best anchors Deterrence's profile\u2014specifically, whether the company aligns more closely with early-stage Seed valuations in the $25M band or commands premium relative valuations more consistent with mid-stage peers. Resolution of this uncertainty requires greater clarity on product maturity, customer traction, and defensibility relative to the comparable set.",
