      "narrative": "Rune Technologies is a Series A defense and security company founded by David Tuttle and Peter Goldsborough that has raised $20M+. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 11 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies\u2014comprised of 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Singularity.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $20M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $40M. Peer-median analysis benchmarks against 11 Defense & Security firms at Series A/B stages. The peer set exhibits wide dispersion\u2014ranging from $125M to $3.0B\u2014with a median valuation of $1.0B, anchored by Series B peers including Dream Security ($3.0B), Allen Control Systems ($2.2B), and Harmattan AI ($1.4B).\n\nThe two methods produce a wide valuation range reflecting stage and maturity heterogeneity within the comp set. The low bound is $34M, the median $520M, and the high bound $1.1B. The spread underscores material uncertainty around Rune's relative positioning within the defense-tech market. Key variables driving final valuation include revenue scale and growth trajectory relative to Series B peers, the company's specific technical differentiation within the sector, and near-term funding milestones.",
