      "narrative": "Biofire, founded by Kai Kloepfer, is a Series A-stage defense and security company that has raised $52.9M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 11 same-sector peers at Series A and adjacent stages, comprising 8 private companies and 2 public entities (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS). Notable private comparables include Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Castelion, alongside Dream Security ($3.0B Series B), Allen Control Systems ($2.2B Series B), and Harmattan AI ($1.4B Series B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses $53M (total raised as proxy for current valuation) with a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $106M. Peer-median analysis across the 11-company comparable set produces $1.0B, with the range spanning $125M to $3.0B, reflecting variance in maturity and defensibility within the defense-tech cohort.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $90M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $553M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty regarding Biofire's competitive positioning relative to more mature Series B peers and the stage-dependent nature of early-stage step-ups. Key sensitivities include revenue traction, technical differentiation within defense applications, and customer concentration risk relative to the peer set.",
