      "narrative": "Umbra is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised over $100M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 4 private peers in the same sector and adjacent stages\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B Series C)\u2014alongside a broader reference set of 5 public space & aerospace companies trading at a median 24.6x price-to-sales.\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base of $100M and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $190M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosure of Umbra's revenue. The wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014driven by differences in funding stage, business maturity, and market segment within aerospace\u2014introduces material uncertainty into the peer-median approach.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $162M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $920M. The gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects early-stage uncertainty and the heterogeneity of the space sector. Public comparable multiples provide directional context but cannot ground a precise estimate absent revenue disclosure. Key uncertainties include Umbra's specific business segment, go-to-market traction relative to named peers, and the sustainability of recent private market valuations in aerospace.",
