      "narrative": "Theseus is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Stanford and McGill-trained engineers, having raised $4.3M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 comparables: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-Progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $11M. Peer-Median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B Seed; Singularity at $400M Series A; NODA AI at $125M Series A) produces a median of $400M, with a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $9M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $205M across both methods. The wide dispersion reflects substantial stage and maturity differences within the peer set. Key uncertainties include the applicability of the Peer-Median method, given that only one comparable is at true Seed stage, and the Stage-Progression method's reliance on a capital-raised proxy rather than revenue or traction metrics. Resolution of these unknowns\u2014particularly evidence of product differentiation, customer traction, or defensibility claims\u2014would materially narrow the valuation band.",
