      "narrative": "NuScale Power operates in the nuclear energy sector, a domain with limited public comparables and a dispersed private funding landscape. The addressable peer universe consists of three public companies and eight private firms pursuing advanced reactor technologies. However, the nuclear energy sector exhibits substantial heterogeneity in technology maturity, regulatory pathways, and capital requirements, which constrains direct comparability.\n\nThe peer-median valuation method is inapplicable to NuScale. The nuclear energy sector contains only six same-stage peers total, and filtering by stage, adjacency, and valuation tier yields fewer than three datapoints\u2014the minimum threshold for robust multiples analysis. Attempting to rely on all-sector medians would obscure material differences in development stage, commercialization risk, and regulatory approval timelines across the peer set. The top private peers identified\u2014Oklo, X-Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, and Nano Nuclear Energy\u2014span wide ranges of funding stage and technology approach, limiting their utility as direct comparables. The three public peers (OKLO, NNE, SMR) provide market reference points but reflect post-IPO valuations subject to distinct liquidity and disclosure regimes.\n\nWithout a sufficient narrow comparable set, triangulated valuation synthesis cannot be completed. A defensible range would require either (1) case-by-case analysis of individual peer transactions with explicit adjustment factors for technology, timeline, and risk profile, or (2) alternative methods such as discounted cash flow or sum-of-the-parts analysis anchored to NuScale's specific project pipeline and regulatory milestones. The $600M+ capital raised to date establishes a floor but does not establish fair value absent forward-looking metrics.",
