      "narrative": "Type One Energy, a Series B nuclear energy company founded by David Anderson, Chris Hegna, and John Canik, operates within a sector represented by 3 public comps (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private peers including Valar Atomics, Helion, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy. The company has raised $100M+ to date.\n\nStage-progression valuation was the applicable triangulation method. Using total raised ($100M) as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to next-stage progression, this method implies a valuation of $190M. Peer-median analysis was not applicable due to insufficient comparables at the same stage and valuation tier within the nuclear energy sector; while six same-sector peers exist, only one same-stage and one adjacent-stage datapoint were identified, falling short of the minimum three-point threshold needed for reliable cross-sectional analysis.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $162M to $218M, with a median of $190M. This range reflects the inherent uncertainty from relying on a single methodological input and the limited availability of tightly filtered peer transactions in the nascent advanced nuclear sector. Key uncertainties include the absence of recent comparable financings at Type One's exact stage and valuation tier, and the broad diversity of technical approaches and commercialization timelines across the peer set, which limits the precision of any stage-based step-up calibration.",
