      "narrative": "Nano Nuclear Energy, founded by Jay Jiang Yu, is a seed-stage nuclear energy company valued at $808M post-money following $600M+ in total fundraising. The nuclear energy sector comprises a comp universe of 3 public peers (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private companies, including Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Fuse Energy.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement to the $808M post-money base, implying a forward valuation of $2.0B. A peer-median approach was not applicable due to insufficient comparable density within narrow stage and tier filters\u2014while 5 nuclear energy peers exist in the broader dataset, same-stage and adjacent-stage cohorts fell below the three-datapoint threshold required for reliable median derivation.\n\nThe analysis supports a triangulated range of $1.7B (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $2.0B. This valuation reflects the company's advanced funding position and sector, but carries material uncertainty around both the appropriate stage-progression multiple for frontier nuclear technology and the absence of sufficient near-peer transaction data to cross-validate the step-up approach. Validation through additional seed or early-stage nuclear transactions would strengthen conviction in this range.",
