      "narrative": "Pacific Fusion is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Will Regan, Keith LeChien, Eric Lander, Carrie von Muench, and Leland Ellison. The company has raised $900M to date. Valuation is triangulated against a comp universe of 11 total peers: 3 public entities (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private companies including Fuse Energy, Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy operating at seed through Series B stages within nuclear energy.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $1.8B. Peer-median analysis across 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Valar Atomics at $6.0B Series B, Nano Nuclear Energy at $808M seed, Fuse Energy at $200M Series A) produces a median of $808M with a range of $200M to $6.0B.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $687M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide dispersion\u2014particularly the $6.0B outlier in the peer set\u2014reflects material uncertainty around stage timing, capital intensity, and technology risk inherent to early-stage nuclear ventures. Key variables for refinement include near-term funding trajectory, technical de-risking milestones, and regulatory pathway clarity.",
