      "narrative": "Outpost Space, founded by Jason Dunn, is a Seed-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $40M+. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE, though the narrow peer set constrains traditional median-based methods.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. Using total raised ($40M) as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier for progression from Seed to Series A, this method implies a valuation of $100M. Peer-median benchmarking proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum threshold (need \u22653 datapoints; only 1 identified at same stage). Public-comp anchoring cannot be executed absent revenue disclosure, though the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 24.6x across the 6 public tickers provides sector context.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $85M to $115M, centered on $100M. This range reflects the stage-progression baseline with modest downside/upside bands applied to acknowledge estimation risk. Key uncertainties include the company's actual near-term revenue trajectory (undisclosed), burn rate relative to raised capital, and the applicability of traditional stage-multipliers to frontier aerospace ventures, which may exhibit non-standard financing patterns. Additional comparable data at similar funding tiers would strengthen conviction.",
