      "narrative": "Proteus Space is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by David Kervin and Andrew Shapiro, having raised $14.4M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates against a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using $17M (total raised as proxy) multiplied by a 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier, implies $34M. Peer-median anchoring across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yields a median of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring was not applicable; the space and aerospace public sector median trades at 24.6x revenue across six tickers, but Proteus Space's revenue is not on file.\n\nThe triangulated range is $29M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $667M. The wide spread reflects fundamental uncertainty about stage-appropriate valuation for a bootstrapped Series A versus market-rate pricing for private space companies at later stages. The stage-progression floor ($34M) anchors downside, while peer-median and upside peer comps define the ceiling. Key uncertainties include actual revenue generation, technical differentiation versus peers, and capital intensity of the business model.",
