      "narrative": "Insitro, a Series C-stage biotech company founded by Daphne Koller, has raised $1.1B+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies in the Biotech & Health sector, including Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. Stage-progression analysis uses the $1.1B total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implying a valuation of $1.9B. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median of $3.8B, with a range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp P/S anchoring cannot be applied due to lack of disclosed revenue for the target.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.6B (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.8B. This wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty around the appropriate peer multiple\u2014driven largely by the $10.3B outlier (Colossal) versus tighter clustering of other private comps. Key uncertainties include the stage-progression multiplier's relevance given rapid frontier-biotech funding dynamics, and whether Insitro's technology differentiation and capital efficiency justify positioning toward the peer-median or higher end of the range.",
