      "narrative": "Eikon Therapeutics is a publicly traded biotech company founded by Luke Lavis, Eric Betzig, Robert Tjian, and Xavier Darzacq. The company's current market capitalization stands at $539M following its IPO, which raised $381M. The valuation universe consists of 3 same-sector, same-stage public peers in Biotech & Health: Recursion Pharmaceuticals ($1.6B), Freenome ($1.1B), and Alto Neuroscience ($1.0B).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach given available data. The median valuation across the 3 public comparables is $1.1B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B. A public-comp anchoring approach using sector price-to-sales multiples (7.4x median across 3 tickers) could not be applied, as the target's revenue is not publicly disclosed. The absence of auditable revenue figures is typical for private-stage biotech and limits multiples-based analysis here.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $935M to $1.3B, centered at $1.1B median. The current public market valuation of $539M sits materially below this peer-derived range, representing a 50% discount to the median. Key uncertainties include post-IPO momentum, clinical trial timelines, and competitive positioning within the biotech peer set. The single-method basis of this analysis reflects data constraints and should be supplemented by revenue trajectory and pipeline stage analysis as additional disclosures become available.",
