      "narrative": "Archer Aviation is a publicly listed autonomous flight platform company in the Drones & Autonomous sector. The valuation analysis is grounded in a peer-median approach across five same-sector comparables spanning development stages from Series B through public: Wayve ($8.6B), Zipline ($7.6B), Joby Aviation ($6.9B), Nuro ($6.0B), and Elroy Air ($800M).\n\nThe peer-median method yields $6.9B, reflecting the central tendency across this heterogeneous valuation range of $800M to $8.6B. This single applicable triangulation method produces an implied valuation of $6.9B. The comparable set is weighted toward later-stage and public entities; the inclusion of Elroy Air at $800M introduces significant dispersion and reflects early-stage capital intensity in autonomous systems development. Archer's current market capitalization of $3.33B sits substantially below the peer median, a gap attributable to commercialization timing, regulatory clearance status, and market sentiment toward autonomous flight platforms.\n\nThe triangulated range\u2014$5.8B (low), $6.9B (median), $7.9B (high)\u2014reflects reasonable bounds given peer volatility. Key uncertainties include regulatory pathway clarity for urban air mobility, near-term revenue visibility, and capital requirements to reach operational scale. The peer set consists of eight private and zero public comparables, limiting cross-validation. Further analysis would benefit from revenue multiples or cash-burn adjusted metrics if available.",
