      "narrative": "Quantum-Systems is a Series D defense and security company founded by Florian Seibel, currently valued at $8.0B post-money following $1.2B in total capital raised. The comparable universe consists of 10 peers: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms operating in the same sector and stage, including Saronic, Chaos Industries, True Anomaly, and Onebrief.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable to this analysis. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the $8.0B last post-money valuation, implying $12.0B at the next funding stage. Peer-median analysis examines 4 same-sector, same-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $2.1B (Onebrief) to $9.2B (Saronic), yielding a median of $3.4B. The divergence between these methods reflects dispersion within the peer set, where the median trails the current valuation by approximately 58%, while Saronic's $9.2B valuation approximates the target's current level.\n\nTriangulating both methods yields a valuation range of $2.8B (low) to $13.8B (high), with a median of $7.7B. The current $8.0B valuation sits near the triangulated median, suggesting reasonable calibration to stage and sector dynamics. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion among peer valuations\u2014a 4.3x spread from minimum to maximum\u2014and reliance on only two methods with limited public market anchoring. Validation against revenue multiples or capital efficiency metrics would strengthen confidence in this range.",
