      "narrative": "**PlanQC Valuation Narrative**\n\nPlanQC is a Series A quantum computing company founded by Alexander Gl\u00e4tzle, Sebastian Blatt, and Johannes Zeiher, having raised $50M+ to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 3 public comparables (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method, using total raised ($50M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression. This yields an implied valuation of $100M. Peer-median analysis was not applicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the quantum computing space; while 8 same-sector peers exist, fewer than three met narrow valuation-tier and stage filters required for reliable median estimation. A broader sector median would introduce excessive noise given the heterogeneity of quantum computing business models and technology approaches.\n\nTriangulation across available methods supports a valuation range of $85M to $115M, with a median estimate of $100M. This range reflects the single applicable method and inherent uncertainty around quantum computing company comparability. Key uncertainties include the trajectory of customer adoption, regulatory environment, and technical differentiation relative to the broader competitor set. Additional financing rounds and revenue traction will refine this estimate considerably.",
