      "narrative": "Verkor is a Series C climate and energy infrastructure company that has raised \u20ac3.0B+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private frontier-tech peers in the climate and energy sector (KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, Amogy, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, and others) plus 1 public comparable (LNZA).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the \u20ac3.0B total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implying a valuation of $5.1B. Peer-median analysis examines three same-stage, same-sector comparables: KoBold Metals ($3.0B), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B), and Amogy ($700M). The median of this peer set is $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThese two methods produce divergent signals, reflecting structural tension between capital-intensity metrics and current market multiples in early-stage climate tech. The triangulated range is $850M to $5.9B, with a median of $3.0B. Key uncertainties center on whether stage-progression assumptions hold given market-rate compression in climate infrastructure valuations and the appropriate precedent weight to assign peers with materially different technology and commercialization timelines. A valuation near the lower quartile of the range may better reflect near-term market conditions.",
