      "narrative": "DNA Script is a Series C-stage biotech company founded by Thomas Ybert that has raised $200M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, with particular focus on 3 same-stage private companies: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $200M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implies $340M. Peer-median valuation across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields $3.8B, with a range of $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 7.4x) could not be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue for the target.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $289M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around DNA Script's current stage maturity, capital deployment pace, and technology validation relative to the peer set. The peer-median estimate appears most reliable given direct comparability, though the stage-progression method's conservative implied value suggests either market conditions have tightened or DNA Script's asset profile lags higher-valued peers. Further clarity on revenue traction, IP position, and capital efficiency would narrow this range materially.",
