      "narrative": "Synhelion, a Series C climate and energy company founded by Gianluca Ambrosetti, is evaluated against a comparable universe of 9 private frontier-tech firms and 1 public entity (LNZA). The peer set\u2014anchored by KoBold Metals ($3.0B), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B), and Amogy ($700M)\u2014represents contemporaneous fundings in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the company's $80M+ total raised as a proxy base, applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implying $136M. The peer-median method references the three same-sector, same-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.0B and a range spanning $700M to $3.0B, reflecting material dispersion in market valuations for this cohort.\n\nTriangulation of these methods produces a range of $116M to $1.1B, with a median of $568M. The wide spread reflects two structural uncertainties: first, material heterogeneity in peer valuations despite stage and sector alignment; second, the sparse and uneven development of comparable data at this technology maturity level. The stage-progression method yields a conservative estimate grounded in capital history, while peer multiples may embed upside assumptions specific to individual companies' technical or commercial trajectories. A defensible valuation likely resides in the $400M\u2013$750M band, conditional on detailed diligence into Synhelion's development milestones and capital efficiency relative to peers.",
