      "narrative": "Saltfoss Energy, a Series A\u2013stage nuclear energy company founded by Troels Schonfeldt, has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector comp universe of 11 peers (3 public, 8 private), including Valar Atomics, Nano Nuclear Energy, and Fuse Energy at comparable stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for post-money valuation, applied a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $80M. Peer-median triangulation across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables produced $808M, calculated from a range of $200M (Fuse Energy, Series A) to $6.0B (Valar Atomics, Series B), with Nano Nuclear Energy (Seed) at $808M serving as the median.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $68M to $929M, with a median of $444M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014notably the inclusion of Valar Atomics at Series B valuation\u2014and reflects inherent uncertainty in early-stage frontier tech valuations. Stage-progression anchors the conservative end; peer comparables drive the upper bound. Key uncertainties include technology maturity relative to peers, capital efficiency, and regulatory pathway clarity, which the current analysis does not quantify.",
