      "narrative": "D-Orbit is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $166M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 13 comparable companies across public and private markets: 5 public-market space and aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Sierra Space, Impulse Space, and Apex Space.\n\nTwo methods apply to this valuation. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $282M. Peer-median analysis benchmarks D-Orbit against 7 same-sector comparables at similar or adjacent stages; that sample spans $1.15B to $8.0B, with a median of $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring using a 24.6x P/S multiple across the 5 public-sector comps is not applicable due to the absence of target revenue disclosure. Public-market comparables in the sector trade at a median 24.6x revenue.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across applicable methods supports a valuation range of $240M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median estimate of $1.1B. The wide range reflects material uncertainty in stage comparability; peer valuations cluster around $2.0B, but D-Orbit's earlier stage and lower capital raised ($166M) versus later-stage peers like Impulse Space ($4.3B) and Sierra Space ($8.0B) suggest a materially lower valuation within the peer sector. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and launch cadence relative to peer benchmarks.",
