      "narrative": "Kyoto Fusioneering is a Series C-stage nuclear energy company founded by Satoshi Konishi that has raised $125M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector universe of 11 comparable companies: 3 public peers (trading under OKLO, NNE, and SMR) and 8 private companies including Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary valuation driver. Using total capital raised of $125M as a baseline proxy, the application of a typical Series C-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 1.7x yields an implied valuation of $212M. This method is grounded in empirical progression patterns at this stage. Peer-median triangulation was not applicable due to insufficient comparable depth: while six same-sector peers exist, the narrow filters for stage, adjacency, and valuation tier yielded fewer than three datapoints, making sector-wide median benchmarking unreliable and potentially misleading.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $181M (low) to $244M (high), with a median point of $212M. This single-method triangulation carries material uncertainty given reliance on stage-progression alone. Key risks to valuation include technology execution risk typical of pre-commercialization nuclear ventures, regulatory pathway clarity, and the limited depth of direct peer comparables at this valuation tier. Investors should weight this range as indicative rather than definitive, pending additional commercial or strategic milestones that would warrant re-benchmarking.",
