      "narrative": "Pixxel, a Series B-stage space and aerospace company, has raised $95M to date. Valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, Skyryse) and 5 public space and aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x to the $95M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $180M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure. The wide dispersion reflects stage and market-position heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014particularly the $8.0B Sierra Space outlier at Series C stage.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $153M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $915M. The gap between stage-progression and peer-median results is material and reflects uncertainty around Pixxel's competitive positioning and revenue trajectory relative to later-stage, higher-valuation peers. Key uncertainties include actual revenue run-rate, customer concentration, and execution risk in a capital-intensive sector. The peer-median approach carries greater weight given relevance of same-stage comparables, though lower-end scenarios warrant consideration if revenue or near-term milestones disappoint relative to peer benchmarks.",
