      "narrative": "SunDrive Solar is a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Vince Allen and David Hu that has raised A$60M+ including a A$25.3M ARENA grant as of November 2025. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of nine private-stage climate and energy firms (including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix) plus one public comparable.\n\nThe analysis applies Stage-Progression methodology, the only triangulation method with sufficient data applicability. Using total raised (A$60M+) as a proxy base of approximately $4M and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier for progression from Seed to next stage yields an implied valuation of $10M. Peer-Median analysis was not applicable due to insufficient narrow-filter peers; while eight Climate & Energy companies exist in the broader comp set, none met same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier criteria in sufficient quantity (minimum three required).\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $8M to $12M, with $10M as the central estimate. Key uncertainties include the limited methodological basis (one applicable method), the absence of tightly-aligned stage peers for cross-validation, and the reliance on total-raised figures as a proxy for valuation benchmarking in an early-stage, grant-funded context. The analysis would benefit from additional comparable data or alternative market-based anchors as the company progresses.",
