      "narrative": "Silicon Box, a Series B chip design company founded by Han Byung Joon, Sehat Sutardja, and Weili Dai, operates within a competitive frontier-semiconductor sector anchored by 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 identified private peers at similar or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using $200M in total raised as a proxy for current enterprise value and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies a $380M valuation. Peer-median triangulation across 4 same-sector companies\u2014Rebellions ($2.3B, Series A), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series A), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014yields a $1.5B median with a range of $529M to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (20.4x median across the three public tickers) cannot be applied, as the target's revenue remains undisclosed.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $323M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $940M across the two applicable methods. This wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Silicon Box's commercialization trajectory relative to its peer set, which spans early-stage AI chip specialists and more mature semiconductor designers. Narrowing this range would require disclosure of revenue run-rate or detailed customer pipeline data.",
