      "narrative": "Satellogic is a public Space & Aerospace company founded by Emiliano Kargieman and Gerardo Richarte. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of five same-sector public peers: SpaceX, Rocket Lab, Planet Labs, Firefly Aerospace, and Astroscale.\n\nThe peer-median approach is the applicable triangulation method given data constraints. The five-company cohort spans valuations from $840M (Astroscale) to $1.6T (SpaceX), with a median of $7.6B. This wide range reflects heterogeneity within the sector\u2014from launch services to on-orbit servicing\u2014but provides the most direct comparator anchor for a public-stage Space & Aerospace business. A Public-Comp P/S method cannot be applied because Satellogic's revenue figures are not on file, though the broader sector median P/S stands at 24.6x across six public tickers.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6.4B (low) to $8.7B (high), centered on a $7.6B median. This reflects peer-derived valuation only; materiality should be weighted against Satellogic's capital raised to date ($262M), business segment positioning within the sector, and growth trajectory relative to comps. Key uncertainties include revenue scale, margins, and addressable market penetration versus the heterogeneous peer set. The wide dispersion in comp valuations ($840M to $1.6T) signals substantial uncertainty in the application of peer multiples to frontier-stage aerospace operators.",
