      "narrative": "Dawn Aerospace, a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $25M to date, sits within a competitive sector encompassing 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and SpaceX. The valuation analysis applies two applicable triangulation methods given available data constraints.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline, applies a typical 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier to the $25M raised, implying a valuation of $48M. The Peer-Median method anchors to a cohort of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (sector median 24.6x across 6 tickers) is inapplicable absent disclosed revenue.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $40M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $849M. The wide dispersion reflects structural uncertainty: the stage-progression floor assumes modest early-stage dynamics, while peer medians embed the sector's substantial valuation variance driven by technical milestone achievement and commercial traction. Key uncertainties include the target's underlying revenue trajectory, technology-stage maturity relative to named peers, and whether peer data reflects recent rounds or stale benchmarks.",
