      "narrative": "Deep Isolation is a Series A nuclear energy company that has raised $26M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 11 companies\u20143 public (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private peers including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Oklo\u2014all operating in the frontier nuclear sector at seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $26M raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A to next-stage step-up, implies a valuation of $52M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $808M, derived from Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A). This method reflects a wide range of $200M to $6.0B, reflecting heterogeneity in maturity and capital deployed within the sector.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a valuation range of $44M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $430M. The wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects uncertainty around Deep Isolation's relative technical progress, market timing, and the nascent stage of commercial nuclear innovation. Key variables include the pace of regulatory advancement, capital intensity of scale-up, and investor appetite for frontier nuclear technologies.",
