      "narrative": "GrayMatter Robotics is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $70M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine private peers\u2014including Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity\u2014plus one public comparable, reflecting the maturity and competitive density of the sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate the range. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the last known post-money valuation of $300M, yielding $570M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables produces $1.8B, with individual valuations spanning $1.6B to $2.0B. The peer set includes Generalist AI at $2.0B, Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, and Dexterity at $1.6B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $484M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The substantial spread reflects meaningful uncertainty around which methodology better captures current market conditions. Stage-progression anchors conservatively to documented historical valuation; peer-median reflects current market pricing for comparable-stage robotics companies but introduces sensitivity to which peers are most relevant. Key uncertainties include revenue traction relative to peers, technology differentiation, and the volatility inherent in private robotics valuations at Series B stage.",
