      "narrative": "Collaborative Robotics, a Series B-stage company in the Robotics & Manufacturing sector founded by Brad Porter, is evaluated against a universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (277810.KQ). The target has raised $150M+ to date.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the last post-money valuation of $500M, yielding $950M. Peer-median analysis uses three same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B)\u2014generating a median valuation of $1.8B and a range of $1.6B to $2.0B.\n\nTriangulation across both methods produces a valuation range of $808M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.4B. The 150-basis-point spread between stage-progression and peer-median reflects both the methodological variance and composition of the peer set. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the three-company peer sample and whether recent stage-progression multiples in robotics reflect current market conditions. The analysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.8B as most defensible given current data.",
