      "narrative": "Chef Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Rajat Bhageria that has raised $65.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private robotics firms and 1 public entity, with leading private comparables including Humanoid, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI across seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy baseline of $15M and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $30M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with the peer set ranging from $1.1B (Walden Robotics, seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B). The five peers include three Series B companies, one Series A, and one seed-stage firm.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide implied range of $26M to $1.9B, with a midpoint of $840M. The substantial divergence reflects fundamental uncertainty around Chef Robotics' market position and growth trajectory relative to the peer set. Stage-progression suggests a more conservative valuation anchored to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects the elevated valuations across the robotics sector. Resolution of this gap depends on clarity around Chef Robotics' unit economics, revenue traction, technical differentiation relative to peers, and near-term fundraising timing.",
