      "narrative": "LeoLabs is a Series B space & aerospace company that has raised $94M to date. The valuation analysis employs a comp universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, Skyryse) alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo methodologies are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $94M raised proxy, yielding $179M. Peer-median analysis across the 4-company cohort produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as LeoLabs does not publicly disclose revenue; the sector median P/S of 24.6x cannot be operationalized without this input. \n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods yields a range of $152M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $914M. This wide dispersion reflects material stage uncertainty: peer valuations span over an order of magnitude, driven partly by differentiation in market traction and capital intensity. Key uncertainties include LeoLabs' revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and competitive positioning within space infrastructure. A tighter valuation would require clarity on near-term revenue run-rate and Series B terms from comparable recent rounds.",
