      "narrative": "Osmo, a Series B consumer tech company founded by Alex Wiltschko, has raised $130M to date. The analysis operates without access to a direct comparables universe\u2014no public peers or private transaction data proved applicable to establish market-based benchmarks for this stage and sector positioning.\n\nGiven the limited methodological toolkit, the valuation relies on stage-progression analysis. Using total capital raised of $130M as a proxy for current enterprise value, a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement yields an implied valuation of $247M. This implies a range from $210M (low) to $284M (high), bracketing the median at $247M.\n\nThe single-method triangulation substantially narrows conviction. The $247M median assumes: (i) total raised is an appropriate proxy for current valuation floor; (ii) a 1.9x multiplier accurately reflects the marginal step-up investors would require at the next financing; and (iii) no material intervening operating performance or market dynamics have shifted since the last capital event. Meaningful refinement would require either comparable transaction data from peer consumer tech Series B rounds or forward-looking operating metrics to stress-test the progression multiple. Absent these, the range should be treated as illustrative rather than prescriptive.",
