      "narrative": "Mission Barns, a Series B biotech company founded by Eitan Fischer and David Bowman, has raised $50M+ to date. Valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private equivalents in Biotech & Health, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression anchored to the $50M total raised proxy applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $95M. Peer-median methodology examined 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies: Colossal Biosciences at $10.3B, Chai Discovery at $3.8B, and New Limit at $3.1B, producing a median of $3.8B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (7.4x median across the three public tickers) was inapplicable due to absence of revenue disclosure. \n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $81M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression implies conservative near-term valuation, while peer-median suggests significant upside if Mission Barns demonstrates comparable clinical or commercial progress to later-stage peers. Resolution of key operational metrics\u2014pipeline advancement, revenue traction, capital efficiency\u2014will materially narrow this band.",
