      "narrative": "FlyBy Robotics is a Seed-stage defense and security robotics company that has raised $5M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public peers in the defense & security sector, including later-stage private companies like UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI, as well as public comparables DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the $5M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $12M. The Peer-Median method examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: UFORCE ($1.0B at Seed), Singularity ($400M at Series A), and NODA AI ($125M at Series A). This yields a median of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in funding outcomes within this sector.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $11M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $206M. The stage-progression floor is conservative and relies on early-stage benchmarking. The peer-median ceiling reflects outliers in a nascent defense-tech market where valuations can vary by an order of magnitude. Key uncertainties include FlyBy's differentiation relative to the peer set, technical validation progress, and addressable market traction\u2014none of which are fully observable at the Seed stage.",
