      "narrative": "Quantinuum, a Series G quantum computing company founded by Ilyas Khan, has raised $2.7B+ and carries a current post-money valuation of $14.8B. The quantum computing sector comp universe includes 10 peers spanning three public companies (IonQ, Rigetti Computing, D-Wave Quantum) and seven private entities, with valuations ranging from $4.5B to $13.0B.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable here. Stage-progression modeling applies a typical 1.25x step-up multiplier from the Series G post-money base, implying $18.5B. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, similar-valuation-tier comparables yields a median of $6.3B, with a range of $4.5B to $13.0B. The peer set includes IonQ at $13.0B, PsiQuantum at $7.0B, D-Wave at $6.3B, SandboxAQ at $5.8B, and Rigetti at $4.5B.\n\nThe triangulation of these two methods produces a valuation range of $5.3B to $21.2B, with a median of $12.4B. The wide spread reflects material tension between stage-progression momentum and peer-relative positioning. Quantinuum's current $14.8B valuation sits above the peer median but within the upper quartile of the comp range, consistent with its later-stage and later-raised-capital profile relative to most peers. Key uncertainties include the timing and terms of potential next-round financing, competitive positioning within the quantum hardware and software stack, and near-term commercialization traction relative to public-market peers.",
