      "narrative": "Wandelbots is a Series G robotics and manufacturing software company founded by Christian Piechnick that has raised $126M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private peers (including Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics) and one public comparable, though narrow peer overlap at this stage and valuation tier limits direct multiples-based triangulation.\n\nStage-progression methodology applies here, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline of $500M and applying a 1.25x step-up multiplier typical for Series G advancement. This yields an implied valuation of $625M. Peer-median analysis was not applicable; while 11 robotics and manufacturing companies exist in the reference set, no subset of three or more comps matched the target's stage, tier, and valuation concurrently, making a narrow peer median unreliable without risking distortion from broader sector comparables.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $531M (low) to $719M (high), with a median of $625M. This single-method result carries execution risk: the stage-progression approach relies on the $500M baseline as a proxy rather than observed market pricing. Key uncertainties include the target's unit economics trajectory, customer concentration, and competitive positioning within the rapidly evolving robotics stack\u2014factors not fully captured by stage-based mechanics alone. Additional data on recent financials or customer retention would materially narrow confidence intervals.",
