      "narrative": "Finwave Semiconductor is a Series A chip design company founded by Tomas Palacios and Bin Lu, having raised $25M+. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 8 private and 3 public semiconductor companies, including Series A stage-peers Rebellions ($2.3B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and Positron AI ($1.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($25M) as a proxy base and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a $50M valuation. Peer-median anchoring across the three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $2.0B midpoint, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples cannot be applied; while the semiconductor sector trades at a 20.4x median P/S across ALAB, NVDA, and AMD, Finwave's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range: $42M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a $1.0B median. This 55x spread reflects tension between stage-based and peer-comparable methodologies. The peer-median approach carries more weight given the direct comparability of Rebellions and d-Matrix at identical stage and sector. Key uncertainties center on Finwave's actual revenue run-rate, customer traction, and burn profile\u2014metrics that would materially narrow the valuation band and anchor toward either the stage-progression or peer-comparable anchors.",
