      "narrative": "Foundry Lab is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $15M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (277810.KQ), weighted toward Series A and B stage robotics and manufacturing firms including Humanoid, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology, anchored to the $15M total raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $30M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The peer cohort spans Seed through Series B stages, reflecting the heterogeneity of available comparables in this frontier sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a low estimate of $26M, a median of $840M, and a high of $1.9B. The wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects structural uncertainty: stage-progression assumes steady capital efficiency, while peer multiples embed significant variations in technology maturity, IP defensibility, and market timing across the robotics sector. Key uncertainties include the degree to which Foundry Lab's technology and burn profile align with the sampled peer cohort, and whether Series A robotics companies are trading at a valuation premium or discount relative to sector-wide median multiples.",
