      "narrative": "Voyant Photonics is a Series A semiconductor company founded by Chris Phare and Steven Miller that has raised $23M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public semiconductor players (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private frontier-chip firms, with immediate peers including Rebellions, d-Matrix, and Positron AI across Series A and adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a $46M valuation. Peer-median anchoring across the 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $2.0B median, with a range of $1.0B (Positron AI, Series B) to $2.3B (Rebellions, Series A). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied: while the Semiconductors peer set carries a 20.4x price-to-sales median, Voyant's revenue remains undisclosed, as is common for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range of $39M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.0B. This dispersion reflects a fundamental tension between valuation based on capital deployed ($46M) and valuation benchmarked to late-stage peer exits. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, technical differentiation relative to named competitors, and whether near-term funding events would reset comparable multiples. A more precise valuation would require disclosure of current run-rate metrics.",
