      "narrative": "Marathon Fusion is a seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Adam Rutkowski and Kyle Schiller that has raised $10.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a nuclear energy sector universe comprising 3 public comps (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private peers including Nano Nuclear Energy, Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the applicable valuation approach here. Using total capital raised of $11M as a proxy for seed-stage value and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $27M. This reflects the standard step-up investors expect when moving from seed funding rounds. Peer-median comparison is not applicable given insufficient depth within Marathon Fusion's narrow peer cohort; while 6 same-sector peers exist in nuclear energy, filtering by stage and valuation tier yields fewer than the three datapoints required for robust median-based analysis.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $23M (low) to $31M (high), centered on a $27M median. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method rather than convergence across multiple approaches. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable transaction data at this stage in nuclear, the early-stage nature limiting financial track record, and sector-wide regulatory and capital intensity variables not captured in raise-size proxies alone.",
