      "narrative": "Remedy Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by David Bell and Jake Sganga that has raised $35M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine private robotics firms and one public company (277810.KQ), including five direct peers at Series A and Series B stages: Humanoid ($1.4B Series A), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a valuation proxy, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical between Series A and subsequent rounds, yielding $70M. Peer-median valuation across the five comparable companies produced $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe wide divergence between methods reflects material uncertainty about Remedy's competitive positioning and capital efficiency relative to the peer set. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively to deployed capital; the peer-median method reflects recent market dynamics in early-stage robotics but lacks stage-specific granularity for Series A. A triangulated range of $60M to $1.9B, with a median of $860M, is supported by the data. Resolution of key uncertainties\u2014unit economics, technology differentiation, and customer traction relative to Humanoid and Walden\u2014will be critical to narrowing this band.",
