      "narrative": "Verdant Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Gabe Sibley and Curtis Garner that has raised $58M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private robotics firms and one public comparable (277810.KQ), with five same-sector peers at Series A and adjacent stages serving as primary anchors: Humanoid ($1.4B Series A), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $58M raised proxy, implying $116M. Peer-median triangulation across the five same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B. This peer set reflects material heterogeneity in stage positioning: three comps are at Series B, one at Series A, and one at Seed.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $99M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $883M. The substantial width reflects tension between the stage-progression method and peer benchmarking. Key uncertainties include whether peer valuations reflect comparable operational maturity and capital efficiency, and whether Verdant's progress metrics and market positioning justify positioning toward the higher end of the peer range or warrant a discount to the median.",
