      "narrative": "Rugged Robotics, founded by Derrick J. Morse and Logan Farrell, is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private robotics firms and 1 public company (277810.KQ), including adjacent-stage peers such as Humanoid (Series A, $1.4B), Bedrock Robotics (Series B, $1.8B), and Dexterity (Series B, $1.6B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x multiplier to the $12M raised proxy, implying a $24M valuation. Peer-median analysis examines 5 same-sector comparables spanning Seed to Series B, with valuations ranging from $1.1B to $2.0B and a median of $1.6B. The peer cohort includes Walden Robotics (Seed, $1.1B), Humanoid (Series A, $1.4B), Dexterity (Series B, $1.6B), Bedrock Robotics (Series B, $1.8B), and Generalist AI (Series B, $2.0B).\n\nThe triangulated range is $20M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $837M. The wide spread reflects material stage and maturity dispersion within the peer set. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor given early-stage capital deployed; peer-median anchors to recent market transactions but includes both upstream (Series B) and downstream (Seed) comparables. Key uncertainties include timing to Series B fundraising, revenue traction relative to peer cohort, and sector-specific valuation compression or expansion in robotics markets.",
