      "narrative": "Aeon Industrial is a Seed-stage company in the Defense & Security sector founded by Naweed Tahmas and Joe Cieslik. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe comprising 10 comparable companies: 2 public entities (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-Progression uses the company's $18.6M total raised as a baseline and applies a typical 2.5x multiplier for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $46.5M. Peer-Median analysis examined three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B Seed, Singularity at $400M Series A, and NODA AI at $125M Series A), establishing a median valuation of $400M with a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $40M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $223M. The substantial spread reflects meaningful uncertainty around stage-appropriate valuation: the Stage-Progression method implies $46.5M, while Peer-Median suggests $400M. This divergence hinges on whether Aeon should be valued closer to typical early-stage capital deployment or at the premium multiples observed within the Defense & Security peer set. Resolution requires clarity on competitive positioning relative to named peers and market traction beyond capital raised.",
