      "narrative": "NVision Imaging Technologies is a Series A biotech company founded by Martin Plenio, Ilai Schwartz, Fedor Jelezko, Alex Retzker, and Sella Brosh, having raised $20M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit, Recursion Pharmaceuticals, and Freenome.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable: Stage-Progression. Using the $20M total raised as a value proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier standard for Series A progression yields an implied valuation of $40M. The Peer-Median approach could not be executed due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparable datapoints within the narrow peer set\u2014while 7 same-sector peers exist, only three public comparables were available for reference, below the threshold for reliable median-based pricing. Public-Comp Anchoring using the sector median P/S multiple of 7.4x was inapplicable because NVision's revenue is not publicly disclosed, a common constraint for private-stage companies.\n\nThe triangulated range is $34M (low) to $46M (high), with a median of $40M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single methodology. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data, which precludes market-multiple validation, and the sparsity of precise stage-matched private comparables for calibration.",
