      "narrative": "Ideon Technologies is a Series B-stage climate and energy company founded by Gary Agnew, having raised $30M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (LNZA), all operating in the Climate & Energy sector at Series B/C stages. Key private peers include KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $30M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B progression, yielding $57M. Peer-median analysis anchors to three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: KoBold Metals at $3.0B (Series C), Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B (Series C), and Amogy at $700M (Series C). The median valuation across these three peers is $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $48M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $528M. The wide range reflects material uncertainty regarding stage-to-stage multiple application relative to peer scaling patterns in the frontier-energy sector. Key risks include the sparse early-stage comp set and the significant valuation dispersion among Series C peers, which limits confidence in extrapolation downward to Series B.",
