      "narrative": "Akash Systems is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies operating in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages, including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this analysis. The stage-progression method, anchoring to the $40M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $76M. The peer-median method examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $1.1B to $8.0B, yielding a median of $1.6B. The public-comp anchoring approach (6 Space & Aerospace tickers trading at a 24.6x median P/S) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue data. The two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range of $65M to $1.9B, with a median of $863M. This dispersion reflects material uncertainty around whether Akash's technology trajectory and market opportunity align with lower-funded, earlier-stage companies or with the more mature, capital-intensive peers in the sample. Key uncertainties include revenue scale, customer traction, and capital efficiency relative to the peer set.",
