      "narrative": "Xsight Labs, a Series D semiconductor company that has raised $281M to date, operates within a competitive cohort of eight private and three public peers spanning chips and semiconductor design. The private peer set\u2014anchored by companies like Tenstorrent, Nearfield Instruments, and Cerebras\u2014exhibits substantial stage and valuation dispersion, ranging from $529M to $5.0B.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to Xsight. Stage-progression analysis, using the $281M raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement, yields $422M. Peer-median valuation across five same-sector comparables (Etched, Ayar Labs, Tenstorrent, Nearfield Instruments, and DEEPX) at $2.7B provides an alternative anchor. Public comparable anchoring\u2014with Semiconductor sector median P/S of 20.4x across ALAB, NVDA, and AMD\u2014remains inapplicable due to absence of target revenue disclosure. \n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.6B median, with $358M low and $3.1B high bounds. The disparity between stage-progression ($422M) and peer-median ($2.7B) reflects Xsight's position relative to later-stage capital raises in the peer set. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, technology differentiation relative to Tenstorrent and Nearfield comparables, and timing to Series E fundraising. The median estimate of $1.6B anchors a defensible valuation pending additional disclosed metrics.",
