      "narrative": "Seneca is a Series A autonomous systems company in the Drones & Autonomous sector, founded by Stuart Landesberg and Nick Foley. The target sector comprises 8 private peers including Waymo, Wayve, Zipline, Joby Aviation, and Nuro, with no public comparables available. A narrow peer-median approach was not feasible due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage datapoints within valuation-comparable tiers.\n\nThe analysis applies Stage-Progression methodology, using Seneca's $60M total raised as a proxy for current enterprise value. This method incorporates a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage progression, yielding an implied valuation of $120M. Peer-median triangulation was inapplicable; the sector contains only 8 private companies, and filtering for stage, timing, and valuation tier produced fewer than the three datapoints required for statistical reliability.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $102M to $138M, with a median of $120M, supported by a single methodology. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 2.0x multiplier for Seneca's specific risk profile and market conditions, and the absence of public market pricing signals. Any valuation within this range should be stress-tested against company-specific traction, unit economics, and macro conditions in autonomous systems funding.",
