      "narrative": "Lunar Outpost is a Series A space technology company that has raised $23.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 5 public Space & Aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 3 private peers at Series B and Seed stages (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Starcloud at $1.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The Stage-Progression method applies a 2.0x multiplier to the $23.6M raised proxy, yielding $47M, reflecting typical step-up multiples from Series A to subsequent funding rounds. The Peer-Median method uses the three same-sector comparables, which span valuations from $1.1B to $2.0B with a median of $1.3B. The Public-Comp Anchoring approach cannot be applied because target revenue is not disclosed, though the public Space & Aerospace median trades at 24.6x P/S across six tickers.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a range of $40M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $674M across the two applicable methods. The wide range reflects stage and maturity dispersion in the peer set: earlier-stage peers and the capital-raise proxy anchor toward the lower end, while later-stage private comparables drive the upper bound. Key uncertainties include the target's revenue trajectory, unit economics in hardware manufacturing, and whether peer valuations reflect recent market corrections in space technology.",
