      "narrative": "Transmutex is a Series A nuclear energy company that has raised $23M to date. The valuation analysis benchmarks against a comp universe of 11 peers across the frontier nuclear sector: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private entities including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy, spanning seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $23M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage progression, implying $46M. Peer-median analysis draws from three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Fuse Energy at $200M (Series A), Nano Nuclear Energy at $808M (Seed), and Valar Atomics at $6.0B (Series B). The median valuation across these three is $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods yields a valuation range of $39M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $427M. The dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage comparability and the early-stage heterogeneity of the nuclear frontier peer set. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively on deployed capital, while peer-median is pulled upward by higher-stage outliers. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to Fuse Energy, the timing and capital intensity of demonstration phases, and regulatory pathway clarity.",
