      "narrative": "Ultima Genomics is a Series C-stage biotech company that has raised over $700M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 3 public comparables in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers, with particular relevance to 3 same-stage private companies: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $700M total raised as a value proxy and applying a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implies $1.2B. Peer-median anchoring across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales could not be applied due to the absence of disclosed revenue for private Ultima.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $1.0B (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median estimate of $2.5B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: the peer set includes substantial outliers (Colossal at $10.3B suggests sector willingness to pay premium multiples for specific therapeutic approaches), and stage-progression relies on a raised-capital proxy rather than direct cash-flow or comparable transaction data. Revenue visibility and clinical-stage risk remain primary drivers of valuation uncertainty.",
