      "narrative": "Manifold Bio is a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Gleb Kuznetsov and Pierce Ogden that has raised $40M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 companies across Biotech & Health (3 public, 8 private), including peers such as Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable given available data. The stage-progression approach anchors to Manifold's $40M total raised and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the subsequent financing round, yielding an implied valuation of $80M. The peer-median method could not be deployed due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow biotech peer set meeting minimum sample thresholds. Public-comp anchoring using the sector's 7.4x price-to-sales median (derived from RXRX, TEM, and ONT.L) could not be applied absent revenue disclosure, which private companies rarely provide.\n\nThe triangulated range is $68M to $92M, with a median of $80M. This narrow band reflects reliance on a single method; the primary uncertainty is Manifold's actual pipeline stage, capital efficiency, and intellectual property strength\u2014factors not quantified in available data. Investors should seek additional diligence on revenue trajectory expectations and competitive positioning within the frontier biotech subsector to refine this estimate.",
