      "narrative": "Strand Therapeutics is a Series B-stage biotech company founded by Becraft, Kitada, and Weiss that has raised $205M to date. The valuation universe comprises 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in Biotech & Health, with near-stage anchors including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit, all valued in the $3.1B\u2013$10.3B range at Series C.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value, applies a typical Series B-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 1.9x against the $205M base, yielding $390M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range of $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (sector median: 7.4x across 3 tickers) is not applicable due to absence of target revenue disclosure, standard for private companies.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods across low, median, and high scenarios produces a range of $331M to $4.4B, with a median of $2.1B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression implies meaningful value creation ahead of Series C, while peer-median anchors to later-stage transactions. Key uncertainties include technology validation progress, clinical-stage advancement, and which peer trajectory Strand most closely tracks.",
