      "narrative": "Heart Aerospace, a Series B-stage space and aerospace company founded by Anders and Klara Forslund, has raised $185M to date. Valuation analysis draws on two applicable methods within a peer universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C).\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $185M raised proxy, implying a $352M valuation. Peer-median anchoring across the 4-company set yields a $1.6B valuation, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public comparables in Space & Aerospace (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trade at a 24.6x median P/S, but this method remains inapplicable absent disclosed revenue.\n\nTriangulating the two viable methods produces a $299M floor and $1.9B ceiling, with a $1.0B median. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and scale variance within the peer set, particularly the inclusion of Series C financings and Sierra Space's outsized valuation. Key uncertainties center on Heart Aerospace's revenue trajectory, customer traction relative to Cowboy Space and Aalyria, and whether nearer-term funding rounds will track toward the peer median or remain anchored to stage-typical multiples of capital raised.",
