      "narrative": "Heron Power is a Series B climate and energy company founded by Drew Baglino that has raised $178M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (LNZA), all operating in the Climate & Energy sector at similar or adjacent development stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised ($178M) as a proxy for Series B valuation and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of B-to-next-stage step-ups, implying a valuation of $338M. The peer-median method examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $700M to $3.0B. These peer valuations reflect the capital intensity and market expectations within frontier climate technology.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a valuation range of $287M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median point of $669M. The wide dispersion between methods\u2014stage-progression anchors conservatively at the $338M level while peer multiples extend substantially higher\u2014reflects structural uncertainty around capital efficiency and path-to-scale within this sector. Key uncertainties include technology de-risking trajectory, competitive positioning relative to the peer set, and how comparable companies' public market performance evolves. The median estimate of $669M offers a defensible midpoint absent material shifts in sector fundamentals.",
