      "narrative": "VEIR, a Series B climate and energy company that has raised $117M to date, is valued using a triangulation of stage-progression and peer-median methodologies against a universe of nine private and one public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA). The peer set includes three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage climate-tech companies: KoBold Metals ($3.0B, Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B, Series C), and Amogy ($700M, Series C).\n\nThe stage-progression method applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $117M total raised as a proxy base, implying a valuation of $222M. The peer-median approach extracts the median valuation of the three comparables at $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. These two methods produce meaningfully different signals, reflecting VEIR's earlier stage relative to its peer set and variation in maturity and capital intensity across climate-tech verticals.\n\nTriangulating these results yields a low of $189M, median of $611M, and high of $1.1B. The wide dispersion between methods reflects genuine uncertainty: stage-progression anchors to capital deployed rather than market-tested comparable multiples, while peer-median relies on limited N and later-stage comps. Key sensitivities include VEIR's pathway to subsequent funding rounds, execution risk relative to peer trajectories, and duration before material revenue inflection.",
