      "narrative": "Mytra is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $200M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private firms and 1 public company operating in robotics and manufacturing at Series B through Series D stages, including Exotec ($2.0B Series D), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Hadrian ($1.6B Series D).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using total raised as a proxy for Series C entry value, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for the Series C-to-D transition, yielding $340M. The peer-median method across seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. These two approaches create tension: stage-progression anchors lower, while peer calibration anchors substantially higher.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a range of $289M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $995M. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty about whether Mytra tracks closer to the lower end of the robotics peer set or commands valuation parity with mid-to-high tier comparables. Resolution depends on Mytra's unit economics, deployment scale, and revenue trajectory relative to named peers. The peer-median method carries greater weight given its direct market comparability, though the stage-progression floor provides a conservative floor.",
