      "narrative": "Hertha Metals is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $17M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private companies and 1 public company operating in the same sector, including adjacent-stage peers such as Humanoid (Series A, $1.4B), Bedrock Robotics (Series B, $1.8B), and Dexterity (Series B, $1.6B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $17M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $34M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B (Walden Robotics, Seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B).\n\nThe wide dispersion between methods\u2014$34M versus $1.6B\u2014reflects material uncertainty in whether pre-revenue or early-revenue status should anchor valuation, and the degree to which late-stage comparable multiples apply to Series A positioning. A triangulated range of $29M to $1.9B encompasses both approaches but is uninformative without additional data on Hertha's revenue traction, unit economics, and competitive differentiation relative to the peer set. Resolution of valuation to a defensible point estimate will require clarity on revenue or near-term revenue visibility.",
