      "narrative": "Tytan Technologies is a Series A-stage defense and security company founded by Balazs Nagy and Batuhan Yumurtaci that has raised \u20ac30M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 11 companies in the Defense & Security sector at the same or adjacent stage, comprising 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Castelion.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach uses total capital raised (\u20ac30M) as a proxy baseline and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, yielding \u20ac60M. The peer-median method examines the 11-company comparable set, which displays a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $125M to $3.0B. Named peers at Series B stage include Dream Security ($3.0B), Allen Control Systems ($2.2B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), and Twenty ($1.0B).\n\nThe two methods produce wide dispersion. Triangulation across both approaches yields a range of $51M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median estimate of $530M. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively; the peer-median method reflects maturation and sector tailwinds in defense tech but introduces significant uncertainty around which peer cohort most appropriately reflects Tytan's current operational and commercial stage. Resolution of this gap requires clarity on revenue, customer concentration, and technology differentiation relative to the named peer set.",
