      "narrative": "HyImpulse is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac74M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comparable set including 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies spanning similar stages, with particular relevance to four same-sector peer valuations: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression, using the \u20ac74M total raised as a proxy baseline with a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, yields \u20ac141M ($141M). Peer-median valuation across the four comparable companies produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via Price-to-Sales multiples cannot be applied because HyImpulse's revenue is not on file. The median P/S across the six public comps is 24.6x, but without disclosed revenue this method does not triangulate.\n\nThese two methods support a valuation range of $120M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $895M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around stage-appropriate valuation; the stage-progression method suggests a more conservative floor, while peer medians reflect the higher multiples commanded by later-stage aerospace entrants. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, technology maturation, and customer traction relative to the peer set.",
