      "narrative": "Reverion, a Series B climate and energy company, has raised $79M to date across five founders. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable set spanning one public company (LNZA) and eight private firms, with particular focus on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers: KoBold Metals (Series C, $3.0B), Electric Hydrogen (Series C, $1.0B), and Amogy (Series C, $700M).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy base and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a value of $150M. Peer-median analysis across the three comparables yields $1.0B, reflecting the range of $700M to $3.0B observed in the peer set. The peer approach is most defensible given the direct sector and stage alignment, though all three comps are one stage ahead (Series C), introducing some upward bias.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a range of $128M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $575M. The wide spread reflects genuine uncertainty: stage-progression anchors conservatively to deployed capital, while peer medians reflect market expectations for companies further advanced in fundraising. Key sensitivities include the trajectory of Reverion's technology commercialization relative to its peer cohort and near-term fundraising dynamics in the climate-tech sector.",
