      "narrative": "Enapter is a publicly listed Climate & Energy company trading on the Frankfurt exchange under ticker H2O. The valuation universe consists of one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers spanning battery materials, advanced energy storage, and hydrogen technologies. The private peer set includes Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix, among others.\n\nThe peer-median method is not applicable to this analysis. While eight same-sector comparables exist within Climate & Energy, none satisfy narrow filtering criteria\u2014requiring either same-stage positioning, adjacent-stage proximity, or similar valuation tier membership\u2014to yield the minimum three datapoints necessary for robust triangulation. A retreat to all-sector median multiples would introduce unacceptable model risk given Enapter's specialized technology positioning and capital intensity relative to broader climate tech cohorts.\n\nThe absence of sufficient narrow peer density reflects structural characteristics of the frontier climate-tech market: early-stage private companies and public listings operate across disparate funding stages and valuations, limiting direct comparability on revenue multiples, FCF yields, or traditional metrics. Without executable peer-median or precedent-transaction methodologies supported by adequate datasets, valuation synthesis requires alternative approaches\u2014including asset-based assessments, discounted cash flow modeling tied to capital deployment schedules, or qualitative frameworks anchored to technology maturity and addressable market size. The key uncertainty remains the availability of audited financial data and forward guidance necessary to anchor quantitative modeling.",
