      "narrative": "Basecamp Research is a Series B biotech company founded by Oliver Vince and Glen Gowers that has raised $85M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public equities (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, with particular emphasis on 3 same-stage Series C companies: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $85M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B-to-later transitions, yielding $162M. Peer-median anchoring across the 3 comparable Series C companies produces a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range of $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not on file; while the Biotech & Health sector median trades at 7.4x price-to-sales across the 3 public tickers, private companies rarely disclose revenue at this stage.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $137M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The wide spread reflects meaningful uncertainty around whether Basecamp's profile clusters nearer the stage-progression baseline or the mature peer set. Further diligence on pipeline stage, IP strength, and burn trajectory would refine placement within this range.",
