      "narrative": "Fractile is a Series B frontier-chip company founded by Walter Goodwin that has raised $220M to date. The valuation universe consists of 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in the same sector and stage cohort, including Positron AI, Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, SambaNova Systems, and Etched.\n\nTwo valuation methods were triangulated. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $220M total raised proxy, yielding $418M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comps (Rebellions at $2.3B, d-Matrix at $2.0B, Positron AI at $1.0B, and DEEPX at $529M) produces a median of $1.5B, with a range of $529M to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (median 20.4x across the three public tickers) could not be applied due to absence of Fractile's revenue figures, which is typical for private-stage companies.\n\nThe two applicable methods support a valuation range of $355M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $959M. The 4.8x spread reflects material uncertainty around whether Fractile should anchor toward capital-deployed proxies or peer valuations skewed by earlier-stage funding rounds. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, competitive positioning within the peer set, and typical dilution expected in the next funding round.",
