      "narrative": "Humanoid, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Artem Sokolov, raised $152M at a $1.35B post-money valuation. The analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public company in robotics and manufacturing, including Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics at adjacent stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A to next-stage advancement, implies a $2.7B valuation from the $1.4B last post-money base. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yielded a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B across the peer set. The disparity reflects stage variance in the peer sample, with two Series B-stage companies at $1.8B and $2.0B and one Seed-stage company at $1.1B.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $1.4B (low) to $3.1B (high), with a median of $2.2B. The current valuation of $1.35B sits at the lower bound, suggesting modest upside under conservative assumptions. Key uncertainties include execution risk at Series A and the timing and magnitude of capital efficiency gains necessary to justify higher multiples relative to peer benchmarks.",
