      "narrative": "Epoch Biodesign is a Series A\u2013stage biotech company founded by Jacob Nathan that has raised $40M to date. The valuation framework draws on a comp universe of 3 public biotech and health companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals, though narrow-stage peer multiples proved insufficient for direct application.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable lens here. Using total capital raised ($40M) as a proxy for Series A valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression yields an implied valuation of $80M. Public comparables in Biotech & Health trade at a median P/S of 7.4x across the three tickers identified, but cannot be deployed without the target's revenue figure, which remains undisclosed. The Peer-Median approach is similarly inapplicable: while 7 same-sector peers exist, none of the filtered cohorts (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier) returned the minimum 3 datapoints needed for reliable triangulation.\n\nGiven the single-method basis for this analysis, the valuation range is necessarily narrow and carries material uncertainty. The analysis supports a range of $68M to $92M, centered on $80M, but this reflects primarily the stage-progression method with no independent validation from peer multiples or revenue anchors. Key uncertainties include the target's clinical stage, IP position, and burn rate\u2014factors material to biotech valuation that are not reflected in this limited dataset.",
