      "narrative": "Blykalla is a Series B nuclear energy company founded by Janne Wallenius and Peter Szakalos that has raised $60M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 peers across the nuclear energy sector\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Valar Atomics, Helion, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy.\n\nA peer-median approach proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the nuclear energy space; only 1 same-stage and 1 adjacent-stage peer existed, falling short of the 3-datapoint threshold needed for reliable cross-sectional analysis. Consequently, the valuation relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B to later-stage transitions against the $60M total capital raised as a proxy baseline. This method yields an implied valuation of $114M.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $97M to $131M, with a median point of $114M. This single-method result carries material uncertainty: the range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression output, but lacks corroboration from revenue, margin, or peer multiple approaches due to limited comparable data at Blykalla's specific stage and valuation tier within frontier nuclear. Investor confidence in this range is contingent on validation through asset-based, market-size, or deal-flow benchmarking outside the peer set.",
