      "narrative": "SatRev is a Series B-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Grzegorz Zwoli\u00ad\u0144ski, Damian Fija\u00ad\u0142kowski, and Rados\u0142aw \u0141apczy\u0144ski. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 4 private companies at Series B and adjacent stages within the same sector, supplemented by observation of 5 public Space & Aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers is $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B (Skyryse, Series C) to $8.0B (Sierra Space, Series C). The immediate peer set includes Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B (Series B) and Aalyria at $1.3B (Series B), both closer stage-matches. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied because SatRev's revenue is not on file; however, the public Space & Aerospace sector trades at a median 24.6x price-to-sales across the 6-ticker sample, providing context for the sector's valuation intensity.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.4B to $1.9B, centered on $1.6B. Key uncertainties include stage-specific discounts (Series B companies typically trade below their Series C peers within the same cohort) and SatRev's unreported revenue or customer traction, both of which would refine positioning within the derived range. The 4-peer sample, while adequate for direction, carries inherent narrowness risk given the frontier-tech sector's heterogeneity.",
