      "narrative": "C12 Quantum Electronics is a Series A quantum computing company founded by Matthieu and Pierre Desjardins. The target sector comprises 3 public companies (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies to this valuation. Using total capital raised of $19.4M as a Series A proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier to subsequent-stage progression yields $38.8M. This method reflects typical valuation expansion between Series A and later funding rounds within the quantum computing sector. Peer-median triangulation proved inapplicable; while 8 same-sector peers exist, insufficient datapoints met narrow filters for same-stage and adjacent-stage comparison (minimum 3 required), rendering broad all-sector median analysis unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $33M to $45M, with a median estimate of $39M. This range reflects a \u00b115% band around the stage-progression central estimate. Key uncertainties include the scarcity of same-stage quantum computing comparables in available datasets, which constrains validation of the step-up multiplier's appropriateness for C12's specific position. Technology inflection point and capital deployment velocity within quantum computing remain material but unquantified variables. A future valuation update incorporating same-stage or adjacent-stage private transactions would materially improve confidence in this range.",
