      "narrative": "Jimmy Energy is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Antoine Guyot and Mathilde Grivet that has raised \u20ac80M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers across the nuclear energy sector\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Valar Atomics, Helion, Fuse Energy, and X-Energy, spanning seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the \u20ac80M raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying a $160M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A)\u2014yields a median valuation of $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B. The wide peer range reflects heterogeneous company maturity and technology readiness within the sector.\n\nThe two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $136M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $484M. The $748M spread reflects material uncertainty around which peer comparables most closely track Jimmy Energy's capital intensity, regulatory pathway, and time-to-revenue profile. Stage-progression suggests a tighter floor, while peer-median reflects the wide dispersion in early-stage nuclear valuations. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to Fuse Energy ($200M, same stage) and capital requirements relative to Series B peer Valar Atomics.",
