      "narrative": "DiamFab is a Seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Khaled Driche, Gauthier Chicot, and Ivan Llaurado. The company has raised \u20ac8.7M to date. The valuation universe comprises 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems, though the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or similar-tier clustering for reliable median extraction.\n\nGiven data constraints, only the Stage-Progression method is applicable. Using total capital raised (\u20ac8.7M, treated as $9M proxy) as a base valuation, a standard 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to Series A yields an implied valuation of $22M. Public comparables in Semiconductors trade at a 20.4x median price-to-sales multiple, but this cannot be anchored without DiamFab's revenue disclosure\u2014standard for private companies at this stage. Private peer median methodology is inapplicable due to insufficient tight-clustering datapoints across stage and valuation tier.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $18M\u2013$25M, centered on $22M. This range is narrow by necessity: it reflects a single applicable method and thus carries material estimation risk. Key uncertainties include the validity of raised capital as a valuation proxy at Seed stage, the appropriate step-up multiplier for the company's specific cohort and sector dynamics, and unmeasured competitive positioning relative to the fragmented private semiconductor landscape.",
