      "narrative": "Kreios Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Adri\u00e1n Senar, Jan Matar\u03cc, Francisco Boira, Adria Barcel\u03cc, Max Amer, and Francisco Bosch. The company has raised \u20ac8M to date. The valuation landscape includes five public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) with a median public P/S of 24.6x, and eight identifiable private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, Sierra Space, ICEYE, and Starcloud.\n\nGiven data constraints, only the stage-progression method is applicable. Using total capital raised (\u20ac8M) as a proxy for valuation, a typical seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x implies a post-money valuation of \u20ac20M. Peer-median triangulation cannot be reliably applied; while 14 same-sector peers exist, none satisfy narrow filtering criteria (same/adjacent-stage and similar-tier), and using all-sector medians would lack specificity. Public-comp anchoring via revenue multiples is not feasible absent disclosed target revenue.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of \u20ac17M to \u20ac23M, with a midpoint of \u20ac20M. This range reflects a conservative 2.1x to 2.9x multiple on capital deployed. Key uncertainties include the company's current revenue run-rate and near-term growth trajectory, both critical to validating this range against public multiples. Additional data on customer traction and product stage would materially refine the valuation.",
