      "narrative": "Pale Blue is a Series A space & aerospace company founded by Jun Asakawa and Yuichi Nakagawa that has raised $7.5M in equity plus $27M in non-dilutive grant funding. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression anchors to the $8M total-raised proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage advancement, implying $15M valuation. Peer-median triangulation across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yields a median of $1.3B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring using the 24.6x sector P/S median across the five public names cannot be applied without Pale Blue's revenue disclosure.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range: $13M (low), $658M (median), and $1.5B (high). This dispersion reflects material uncertainty in stage-appropriate valuation multiples and peer comparability. The stage-progression floor reflects minimalist interpretation; the peer-median ceiling reflects early-stage positioning within a high-value sector. Revenue visibility and technical progress toward commercialization are critical valuation drivers not captured in current data.",
