      "narrative": "EX-Fusion is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Kazuki Matsuo, Shinsuke Fujioka, and Yoshitaka Mori that has raised $37M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers across the nuclear energy sector: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Valar Atomics, Helion, X-Energy, Fuse Energy, and Oklo.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $37M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a $74M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A)\u2014yields a median valuation of $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B. The wide peer range reflects heterogeneity in stage and technology maturity within the sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $63M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $441M across the two methods. Material uncertainties center on technology differentiation relative to the Fuse Energy comparable (Series A, $200M) and the trajectory assumptions embedded in the stage-progression multiplier. The peer set's wide dispersion ($200M\u2013$6.0B) underscores sector-specific risk in valuation anchoring.",
