      "narrative": "Dhruva Space is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20b927 crore to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Sierra Space at $8.0B Series C, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Skyryse at $1.1B Series C) alongside a public-market reference set of five Space & Aerospace traded companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring on the \u20b927 crore total raised as a proxy for early valuation and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $51 million. Peer-median analysis across the four private comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6 billion, with observed range spanning $1.1 billion to $8.0 billion. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as Dhruva Space's revenue is not disclosed. The triangulated analysis across the two applicable methods produces a range of $44 million (low) to $1.9 billion (high), with a median of $825 million. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty regarding Dhruva Space's revenue base, customer traction, and technological differentiation relative to peers. Stage-progression alone suggests meaningfully lower valuation than peer median, suggesting either significant near-term operational milestones or downside sensitivity if revenue realization lags peer-comparable growth trajectories.",
