      "narrative": "GalaxEye is a Series A space & aerospace company founded by Suyash Singh and Kishan Thakkar that has raised $10M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression uses the $10M raised as a proxy base and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $20M. Peer-median anchors to 3 same-sector comparable companies at Series B and Seed stages: Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Aalyria ($1.3B), and Starcloud ($1.1B), producing a median of $1.3B and a range of $1.1B\u2013$2.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; the Space & Aerospace public sector trades at a 24.6x median price-to-sales across 6 tickers, but GalaxEye's revenue is not on file.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce divergent results, reflecting stark stage and maturity gaps. The triangulated range is $17M (low), $660M (median), and $1.5B (high). The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around GalaxEye's path to revenue, capital efficiency relative to later-stage peers, and market timing. Stage-progression favors early-stage growth assumptions; peer-median reflects realized valuations in a maturing but capital-intensive sector. Revenue visibility and near-term funding requirements are critical to narrowing this band.",
