      "narrative": "Gilmour Space Technologies is a Series D-stage space and aerospace company that has raised approximately A$100M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, with direct peer comparables limited to 3 same-stage companies in the sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the A$100M total raised as a proxy base value and applying a typical 1.5x Series D step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of A$150M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables (Impulse Space at $4.3B, Apex Space at $2.3B, and Varda Space Industries at $1.6B) yields a median valuation of $2.3B, with a range of $1.6B to $4.3B. Public comparable anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue for the target.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is A$128M (low) to A$2.6B (high), with a median of A$1.2B. The wide spread reflects material dispersion in peer valuations and tension between the stage-progression method and peer multiples. Key uncertainties include revenue generation trajectory, technology maturity relative to peers, and whether peer valuations reflect sustainable market fundamentals or stage-driven investor appetite in the space sector.",
