      "narrative": "Greenroom Robotics is a Series A-stage company in the Defense & Security sector. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 11 same-sector and adjacent-stage companies, comprising 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Singularity.\n\nThe peer-median method, the applicable triangulation approach here, yields $1.0B. This median is derived from an 11-company cohort spanning $125M to $3.0B, with representative Series B peers including Dream Security at $3.0B, Allen Control Systems at $2.2B, Harmattan AI at $1.4B, Code Metal at $1.2B, and Twenty at $1.0B. The consistency of this metric across a reasonably sized peer group suggests limited distortion from outliers.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $850M to $1.1B, centered on $1.0B. Key uncertainties include the one-method limitation of this analysis\u2014peer multiples alone cannot account for Greenroom's specific technology differentiation, customer traction, or burn trajectory. The wide peer range ($125M\u2013$3.0B) also signals substantial heterogeneity within the Defense & Security venture landscape, making any point estimate sensitive to how closely individual comparables mirror Greenroom's profile. Additional methods anchored to revenue multiples, customer acquisition costs, or defensibility metrics would strengthen conviction in this valuation band.",
