      "narrative": "QuamCore, a Series A quantum computing company founded by Alon Cohen, has raised $35M to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 3 public comparables (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nStage-progression methodology is applicable here: using total raised ($35M) as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to subsequent stage, the analysis implies a valuation of $70M. Peer-median triangulation is not applicable\u2014while 8 same-sector private peers exist, insufficient narrow-stage and similar-tier comparables (fewer than 3 datapoints meeting both filters) preclude reliable median derivation. Drawing from the full-sector median would introduce unacceptable heterogeneity given the early stage and nascent market maturity of quantum computing.\n\nBased on stage-progression methodology alone, the analysis supports a valuation range of $60M to $80M, with a central estimate of $70M. This reflects typical Series A markup dynamics. Key uncertainties include capitalization table structure, burn rate, technical milestones achieved, and the timing and terms of the next funding event. The narrow methodological base\u2014reliance on a single applicable technique\u2014underscores the valuation risk inherent in quantum computing at early stages, where performance differentiation and market trajectory remain highly uncertain.",
      "lastUpdated": "2026-09-13T14:31:02+00:00"
