      "narrative": "Majestic Labs is a Series A\u2013stage semiconductor company founded by Ofer Shacham, Sha Rabii, and Masumi Reynders, having raised $100M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public semiconductors (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers, including Rebellions, d-Matrix, Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression anchored to the $100M total raised proxy and applied a typical 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier, implying $200M. Peer-median triangulation across 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Rebellions ($2.3B Series A), d-Matrix ($2.0B Series A), and Positron AI ($1.0B Series B)\u2014yielded a median of $2.0B, with a range of $1.0B to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure, typical for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $170M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.1B. This wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression implies a tighter band near $200M, while peer comparables suggest substantially higher valuations at $2.0B median. Key uncertainties include the strength of Majestic's product differentiation relative to named peers, capital efficiency trajectory, and whether raised capital translates to revenue traction commensurate with later-stage semiconductor valuations.",
