      "narrative": "NordSpace is a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Rahul Goel that has raised $38M+. The valuation universe includes 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning similar stages and the broader space sector, including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo methods triangulate NordSpace's value. Stage-progression applies a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $38M raised as a valuation proxy, implying $76M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The three peers\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014bracket the market positioning. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; the sector median P/S multiple is 24.6x across six public tickers, but NordSpace's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $65M to $1.5B, with a median of $688M. The wide dispersion reflects uncertainty about NordSpace's revenue scale and execution trajectory relative to peers. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor anchored to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects the higher valuations commanded by comparable-stage competitors. Key uncertainties include whether NordSpace's operational metrics and market position align with Series B-stage peers or earlier-stage benchmarks.",
