      "narrative": "Simera Sense is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company founded by Johann du Toit that has raised $16.3M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse) and 5 public space and aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate meaningfully. Stage-progression methodology applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $16M raised proxy, implying a $31M valuation consistent with Series B advancement patterns. Peer-median anchoring across the 4 comparable companies yields a $1.6B median valuation, with the peer set ranging from $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). Public-comp anchoring was not applied; while the space and aerospace sector trades at a 24.6x median price-to-sales multiple across six tickers, Simera Sense's revenue is not disclosed and therefore cannot support this method.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $26M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $840M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Simera Sense's revenue trajectory and competitive position relative to both mature and contemporaneous peers. Stage-progression and peer-median methods yield divergent results; the peer-driven estimate assumes performance and market positioning closer to Series B/C-stage benchmarks, while stage-progression reflects historical funding progression mechanics.",
