      "narrative": "Terrahaptix, a Defense & Security seed-stage company founded by Nathan Nwachukwu and Maxwell Maduka, has raised $52M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 companies spanning public equities (2 public companies: DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private Defense & Security firms at seed and Series A stages, including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $52M in total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yields $130M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A)\u2014produces a median valuation of $400M, with a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $110M to $460M, with a median of $265M across both methods. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty in stage-appropriate benchmarking within the Defense & Security frontier-tech subset. Stage-progression and peer multiples diverge significantly, driven by heterogeneous comparable growth profiles and fundraising environments. Key sensitivities include peer selection tightness at seed stage and assumed step-up multiplier persistence in the current market environment.",
