      "narrative": "Morpheus Space is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Daniel Bock and Istv\u00e1n L\u0151rincz, having raised $43M+ to date. The valuation framework draws on a comparable universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, with 3 directly applicable same-sector and adjacent-stage private comparables (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B Series B; Aalyria at $1.3B Series B; Starcloud at $1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo quantitative methods are applicable. Stage-progression uses the $43M total raised as a proxy base valuation and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying $86M. Peer-median anchors to the three same-sector comparables, which show a median valuation of $1.3B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; the sector shows a median P/S multiple of 24.6x across 6 tickers, but Morpheus Space's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated range is $73M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $693M derived from the two applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects tension between the stage-progression method anchored to capital deployed and the peer-median approach weighted toward later-stage comparable valuations. Key uncertainties include whether private peer selections appropriately reflect Morpheus Space's specific technology maturity, market traction, and capital efficiency relative to the raised base.",
