      "narrative": "Atmos Space Cargo is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac30M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 5 public-traded space companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 3 private peers at Series B and adjacent stages: Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Aalyria ($1.3B), and Starcloud ($1.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x multiplier to the \u20ac30M raised proxy, implying \u20ac60M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables yields a \u20ac1.3B median valuation, with a range of \u20ac1.1B to \u20ac2.0B. Public-comp anchoring using a 24.6x P/S median across the five public tickers cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue for the target.\n\nThe triangulated range spans \u20ac51M to \u20ac1.5B, with a median of \u20ac680M across the two applicable methods. This wide spread reflects the inherent dispersion between the stage-progression method (conservative, capital-based) and peer multiples (market-based, reflecting sector momentum). Key uncertainties include whether Atmos's operational milestones and technical differentiation align it toward the upper peer range or whether near-term capital intensity and execution risk justify a discount closer to the stage-progression floor. Additional disclosure of revenue guidance or customer commitments would narrow this band substantially.",
