      "narrative": "Orbem is a Series B biotech company founded by Pedro G\u00f3mez, Maria Laparidou, and Miguel Molina Romero. The company has raised \u20ac55.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 11 companies across Biotech & Health\u20143 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $56M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $105M. The Peer-Median method uses three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $3.8B (range: $3.1B\u2013$10.3B), reflecting the wide dispersion in early-stage biotech valuations. Public-Comp Anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not disclosed. This is typical for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $90M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty: the Stage-Progression method anchors to capital raised and assumes standardized markup factors, while the Peer-Median method incorporates heterogeneous clinical stage, IP position, and capital efficiency across the peer set. Resolution of this range requires clarity on Orbem's clinical advancement, IP defensibility, and burn profile relative to peers.",
