      "narrative": "Space Machines Company is a Series A frontier aerospace firm that has raised AU$11M to date. The valuation framework draws from a comparable universe of 5 public space & aerospace equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector, with three directly applicable private comparables at Series B and Seed stages: Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo quantitative methods triangulate the valuation. Stage-progression methodology applies a 2.0x multiplier to the $11M capital raised proxy, yielding $22M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the three same-sector comparables, which show a median valuation of $1.3B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring using the sector's 24.6x P/S median cannot be applied due to the absence of target revenue disclosure, typical for private companies at this stage. The triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $19M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $661M.\n\nThe wide dispersion reflects material stage and scale heterogeneity within the peer set. The stage-progression floor of $22M represents conservative early-stage positioning, while peer comparables suggest substantially higher valuations conditional on traction and capital intensity. Key uncertainties include target revenue trajectory, capital requirements relative to peers, and the degree to which Series A stage justifies the valuation multiple applied to later-stage comparables.",
