      "narrative": "Lightelligence is a public-stage semiconductor company that has raised $310M+ to date. Valuation analysis relies on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same-stage public comparables: Cerebras ($39.2B), Credo Semiconductor ($35.8B), Ouster ($2.3B), and Aeva Technologies ($1.1B). The broader semiconductor peer universe includes 3 additional public tickers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers.\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across the 4 public semiconductor comparables is $19.0B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $39.2B. This dispersion reflects meaningful variance in market positioning and scale within the frontier-chip segment. Revenue-based multiples (P/S median of 20.4x across ALAB, NVDA, AMD) cannot be applied absent disclosure of Lightelligence's revenue, a typical constraint for private company analysis.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $16.2B (low) to $21.9B (high), centered on a median of $19.0B. Key uncertainties include the material valuation spread within the peer set\u2014a 35x delta between floor and ceiling\u2014and the absence of revenue visibility to anchor relative valuation. Given the single-method derivation, confidence in precision is limited; the range should be interpreted as indicative of order of magnitude rather than a point estimate.",
