      "narrative": "Portal Space Systems is a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Thornburg, Vorbach, and Ravindran, having raised $62.85M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates two applicable methods across a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement, anchoring on the $63M raised proxy to imply $126M valuation. Peer-median analysis draws on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Cowboy Space at $2.0B (Series B), Aalyria at $1.3B (Series B), and Starcloud at $1.1B (Seed), yielding a median of $1.3B with a range of $1.1B\u2013$2.0B. Public-comp anchoring using the 6-ticker Space & Aerospace P/S median of 24.6x cannot be applied; Portal's revenue is not publicly disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $107M (low), $713M (median), to $1.5B (high). This wide spread reflects material methodological tension: stage-progression assumes conservative progression from capital deployed, while peer-median suggests Portal commands valuations aligned with more mature, capital-intensive space players. Key uncertainties include Portal's revenue, path-to-profitability assumptions embedded in peer valuations, and whether the peer set (predominantly Series B stage) adequately reflects Series A positioning. Further diligence on unit economics and market capture thesis would narrow this range.",
