      "narrative": "Scout Space, a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Eric Ingram and Sergio Gallucci, has raised $18M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, with particular focus on 3 same-sector, adjacent-stage private comparables.\n\nTwo triangulation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $18M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-subsequent-stage progression, implies a valuation of $36M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector comparables (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Starcloud at $1.1B Seed) yields a median of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied due to absence of target revenue data, which is standard for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $31M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $668M. The wide dispersion reflects tension between stage-appropriate pricing ($36M) and peer valuations in the $1.1B\u2013$2.0B band. Key uncertainties include the target's revenue traction, competitive positioning within the peer set, and whether the peer comps accurately reflect Scout Space's market position and development stage.",
