      "narrative": "Genesis Therapeutics is a Series B biotech company that has raised $280M+ to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 3 public-sector peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage biotech firms, with particular relevance to 3 same-sector, adjacent-stage comparables: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B Series C), and New Limit ($3.1B Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis uses the $280M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to next-stage advancement, implying a valuation of $532M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the 3-company median valuation of $3.8B, though the range across comparables spans $3.1B to $10.3B, reflecting substantial heterogeneity in the biotech space. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 7.4x across 3 tickers) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures from the target.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $452M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.2B. Stage-progression yields the conservative bound, while peer medians anchor the upper half. Key uncertainty remains the wide valuation dispersion among Series C comparables\u2014a $7.2B gap between floor and ceiling\u2014reflecting stage-specific risk, pipeline quality, and capital efficiency variation typical of early-stage biotech. Revenue visibility and clinical advancement stage relative to peers would refine the range.",
