      "narrative": "Sagence is a Series B chip design company founded by Vishal Sarin, operating within a semiconductor sector universe of 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers. The private peer set includes adjacent-stage companies like Positron AI (Series B, $1.0B) and earlier-stage players such as Rebellions and d-Matrix (both Series A, $2.3B and $2.0B respectively).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to Sagence's $58M total raised, implying $110M. Peer-median anchoring across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $1.5B median valuation, with a range of $529M to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 20.4x across the three public tickers) cannot be applied because Sagence's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulation of these two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $94M to $1.7B, with a median of $805M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression assumes minimal stage-to-stage step-up typical of early funding rounds, while peer-median is pulled upward by recent Series A rounds in the frontier-chip space commanding elevated multiples. Key uncertainties include Sagence's actual revenue trajectory (unobserved), capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether frontier semiconductor funding dynamics support the higher peer valuations or correct toward the stage-based floor.",
