      "narrative": "Performance Drone Works, a Series B defense and security company founded by Ryan Gury, has raised $110M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers in the same sector and stage, including Dream Security ($3.0B), Allen Control Systems ($2.2B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), and Twenty ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $209M. Peer-median valuation across the 8 same-stage, same-sector private comparables stands at $1.1B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B. This spread reflects material heterogeneity within the defense tech subsector at Series B maturity.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $178M (low), $667M (median), to $1.3B (high). The median estimate of $667M sits materially below the peer median, reflecting Performance Drone Works' earlier position in the capital stack relative to the most mature cohort. Key uncertainties include the company's revenue, margin profile relative to named peers, and whether its drone-specific focus commands a valuation premium or discount within the broader defense ecosystem.",
