      "narrative": "Cambium, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Simon Waddington and Stephan Herrera, has raised $127M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-stage, same-sector private companies (Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity) supplemented by a broader universe of eight private comparables and one public reference.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach, using total capital raised as a proxy base, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $241M. The peer-median method captures the median valuation across the three most directly comparable firms at $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.6B to $2.0B. This substantial spread reflects heterogeneity in comparable company trajectories and capital efficiency within the robotics sector.\n\nThe combined analysis supports a valuation range of $205M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $996M. This wide range reflects two distinct interpretative frameworks: a capital-based floor and a peer-market ceiling. Key uncertainties include unit economics relative to the peer set, technology differentiation within manufacturing robotics, and the degree to which recent-stage peer valuations reflect rational market pricing versus sector-wide momentum. Further diligence on Cambium's revenue run rate and gross margins relative to Bedrock Robotics and Dexterity would tighten the range materially.",
