      "narrative": "Sunflower Labs is a Series B autonomous systems company in the Drones & Autonomous sector, having raised $41.7M to date. The relevant peer universe comprises eight private companies operating in the same sector, including Elroy Air, Waymo, Wayve, Zipline, and Joby Aviation. No public comparables exist in this narrow segment.\n\nGiven the early-stage nature of the sector and limited public benchmarks, a peer-median approach is not applicable. The narrow peer set for Series B drones companies yields insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage datapoints to support reliable multiples-based triangulation. Consequently, the analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $42M total-raised proxy. This multiplier reflects typical valuation progression from Series B to subsequent funding stages and yields an implied valuation of $79M.\n\nThe triangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $67M (low) to $91M (high), with a median point of $79M. This range incorporates only one methodological approach, reflecting data constraints in this emerging sector. Key uncertainties include the absence of proven public market comparables, limited visibility into near-term profitability or revenue scaling within the autonomous systems space, and founder track record differentiation relative to the broader peer cohort. A fuller valuation would benefit from revenue or ARR multiples once the company reaches material scale.",
