      "narrative": "Keen Technologies is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by John Carmack that has raised $20M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private robotics and manufacturing firms and one public comparable (277810.KQ), though direct peer matching within the seed stage proved limited.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable approach, applying a 2.5x multiplier to the $20M raised as a valuation proxy, yielding $50M. The Peer-Median method could not be reliably applied; while eleven same-sector peers exist in robotics and manufacturing, the narrow filters for stage, timing, and valuation tier produced fewer than three datapoints necessary for a meaningful median. Using the full-sector cohort would introduce excessive dispersion and reduce analytical precision.\n\nThe triangulation, based on the single applicable method, supports a valuation range of $42M (low) to $57M (high), with a median point of $50M. The narrow range reflects reliance on a single methodology rather than convergence across multiple independent approaches. Key uncertainties include the absence of tightly comparable seed-stage peers in the robotics sector, which limits validation of the 2.5x step-up multiplier in this specific context, and the limited public market data available for sector calibration. Additional revenue or customer traction data would strengthen confidence in this estimate.",
