      "narrative": "ISEE, a Series B stage company in Drones & Autonomous Systems founded by Yibiao Zhao, has raised $70M to date. The valuation universe for this sector comprises 8 private companies including peers such as Elroy Air, Waymo, Wayve, Zipline, and Joby Aviation; no public comparables exist in this narrow subsector.\n\nGiven the limited peer set, only one valuation method proved applicable. The Stage-Progression approach uses the $70M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B to subsequent-stage transitions, yielding an implied valuation of $133M. A peer-median approach was not feasible due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage datapoints within the Drones & Autonomous category\u2014only one same-stage comparable was identified, falling short of the three-point minimum required for reliable cross-sectional analysis.\n\nThe triangulation analysis, constrained to a single applicable method, supports a valuation range of $113M (low) to $153M (high), with a median point of $133M. The primary uncertainty stems from the narrow methodological foundation: reliance on a single stage-progression calculation without peer validation limits confidence in precise value placement. Additional validation through revenue or growth rate comparables, should such data become available, would strengthen conviction in this range.",
