      "narrative": "Alpha School is a Series A AI & Software company founded by MacKenzie Price and Brian Holtz. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (Palantir, ticker PLTR), with particular focus on four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies: Reflection AI ($25.0B Series A), Physical Intelligence ($5.6B Series B), Black Forest Labs ($3.2B Series B), and Field AI ($2.0B Series B).\n\nThe peer-median method, the primary applicable triangulation approach given available data, yields a median implied valuation of $4.4B across the four-company peer set. The range spans $2.0B to $25.0B, reflecting significant dispersion within the AI & Software frontier-tech segment. Given this dispersion, the triangulated valuation range is anchored at a median of $4.4B, with a low estimate of $3.8B and a high estimate of $5.1B, representing a \u00b115% sensitivity band around the median.\n\nKey uncertainties center on Alpha School's differentiated positioning relative to the peer cohort\u2014particularly its competitive standing against Reflection AI's outlier $25.0B valuation and the three Series B comparables clustered in the $2.0B\u2013$5.6B band. Without stage-normalized revenue multiples, ARR, or product-market validation metrics, the analysis reflects peer valuation levels only. A valuation range of $3.8B\u2013$5.1B is supported by current peer data, though material variance should be expected pending disclosure of Alpha School's growth and traction metrics.",
