      "narrative": "9 Mothers is a Seed-stage defense and security company founded by Russell Smith, Roman Khomenko, and Bogdan Pyzh. The company has raised $4.5M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public frontier-defense firms, including Seed and Series A stage peers such as UFORCE ($1.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression applies a 2.5x multiplier to the $4.5M raised as a proxy for current value, implying an $11M valuation reflecting typical Seed-to-next-stage expansion. Peer-Median benchmarks against three same-sector and adjacent-stage comparables, yielding a $400M median valuation with a range of $125M to $1.0B. The methodological divergence reflects both the early-stage opacity of 9 Mothers' metrics relative to later-stage peers and the wide dispersion within the defense-tech sector at growth stages.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $10M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $206M. The gap between methods reflects material uncertainty: Stage-Progression anchors to capital deployed; Peer-Median reflects sector momentum and later-stage benchmarks. Key uncertainties include 9 Mothers' revenue traction, customer pipeline, and defensibility relative to the peer set. Resolution of these operational metrics will be critical to narrowing the valuation range as the company progresses toward Series A.",
