      "narrative": "Citra Space Corporation is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private firms spanning commercial launch, imaging, and satellite communications.\n\nTwo methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x multiplier to the $15M total raised as a proxy for current value, implying a $30M valuation. Peer-median analysis references three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B (Series B), Aalyria at $1.3B (Series B), and Starcloud at $1.1B (Seed). The median across these three peers is $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median: 24.6x across the five public tickers) could not be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure, typical for private companies. \n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $26M to $1.5B, with a median of $665M across the two applicable methods. This wide spread reflects fundamental uncertainty in stage-to-stage progression and peer comparability. The stage-progression floor assumes minimal value creation post-raise; the peer-median ceiling assumes Citra will achieve scale and performance closer to Series B/C benchmarks. Key unknowns include product-market validation, technology differentiation, and management track record relative to the peer set.",
