      "narrative": "Lambda, a Series E AI & Software company that has raised $3.15B to date, operates within a competitive sector populated by 1 public comparable (Palantir) and 8 private peers including Figure AI, Scale AI, and Applied Intuition. The limited availability of same-stage comparables at Lambda's scale constrains the peer-median approach.\n\nValuation analysis relies primarily on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 1.4x step-up multiplier typical of Series E advancement to the $3.1B total raised proxy, yielding $4.4B. The peer-median approach is not applicable due to insufficient narrow-set datapoints; only 1 adjacent-stage peer and 0 same-stage peers meeting filtering criteria exist, falling short of the minimum 3-datapoint threshold required for reliable triangulation. A broader sector median would risk introducing too much heterogeneity given Lambda's capital scale and stage positioning.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $3.7B (low) to $5.1B (high), with a median of $4.4B. This range reflects typical late-stage venture step-ups but carries meaningful uncertainty given reliance on a single quantitative method and the absence of tighter peer anchors. Key risks to valuation include the wide dispersion in late-stage AI company outcomes and the sector's sensitivity to near-term funding environment shifts. Further clarity on Lambda's revenue scale, unit economics, and customer concentration would substantially refine this estimate.",
