      "narrative": "TurbineOne, founded by Ian Kalin and Matt Amacker, is a Series B-stage defense & security company currently valued at $300M post-money following $58M in total capital raised. The valuation analysis draws from a comparables universe of 10 companies (2 public, 8 private) operating in the same sector and stage, including Dream Security ($3.0B), Allen Control Systems ($2.2B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), and Twenty ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, benchmarking typical Series B advancement dynamics, applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $300M current valuation, implying $570M. Peer-median analysis across the 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.2B, with observed peer valuations ranging from $1.0B to $3.0B. These methods produce a low implied value of $484M, a median of $910M, and a high of $1.4B.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $484M to $1.4B, with a midpoint of $910M. The gap between stage-progression ($570M) and peer median ($1.2B) reflects material uncertainty around whether TurbineOne's current market position and capital efficiency align with the higher-valued peer cohort or represent earlier-stage risk. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory relative to peers and customer concentration in defense procurement cycles.",
