      "narrative": "Gallatin AI is a Seed-stage defense and security AI company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private players including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI, all operating in the same sector and at Seed or Series A stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value, applies a typical 2.5x multiplier for advancement from Seed to next stage, implying a $38M valuation. Peer-median analysis draws from three same-sector comparables spanning Seed and Series A stages\u2014UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M\u2014yielding a median of $400M, with a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $32M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $219M. This wide band reflects material uncertainty around stage-typical multiples and peer selection within a sector where valuations span an order of magnitude. Key uncertainties include the applicability of public defense comparables to early-stage private deployment, the heterogeneity of business models across the peer set, and whether current Seed-stage metrics justify upper-quartile positioning relative to the identified universe.",
