      "narrative": "TrustPoint is a seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Patrick Shannon (CEO) and Chris DeMay (COO) that has raised $6.5M to date. The relevant comp universe includes 5 public Space & Aerospace players (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector, though meaningful narrow-stage comparables remain sparse.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using total raised ($6.5M) as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $16M. Peer-median analysis was not feasible due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the Space & Aerospace universe; while 14 same-sector companies exist, none of the refined filters yielded three or more datapoints. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied because target revenue is not disclosed\u2014standard practice for private companies\u2014and without this metric, the 24.6x median P/S across public comps cannot be meaningfully deployed.\n\nThe single applicable method supports a valuation range of $14M to $19M, with a central estimate of $16M. Key uncertainties include the scarcity of peer data at this stage, the absence of revenue disclosures necessary for public-comp triangulation, and reliance on a stage-progression step-up that assumes typical capital efficiency. Additional data on customer traction or technology differentiation would improve conviction in this range.",
