      "narrative": "Ample, a Series C-stage climate and energy company founded by Khaled Hassounah and John De Souza, has raised $720.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), supplemented by a broader universe of 8 private climate-tech companies and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yields $1.2B. Peer-median valuation across the three directly comparable Series C firms produces $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. These methods converge on overlapping guidance.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $850M (low) to $1.4B (high), with a median of $1.1B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion within the peer set\u2014a 4.3x spread between floor and ceiling\u2014reflecting heterogeneity in underlying business models and stage maturity within climate tech. The modest peer sample size (n=3) and absence of recent public comps in the immediate subsector limit confidence in either tail of the range. Capital efficiency and unit economics trajectory will materially influence positioning within this band.",
