      "narrative": "Loyal is a Series C biotech company that has raised $250M+ to date. Valuation analysis triangulates across two applicable methods: stage-progression multiples and peer median positioning within a narrow same-stage, same-sector comp set of three private companies (Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit). A third method anchoring to public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) cannot be applied due to lack of target revenue disclosure.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $250M raised proxy, implying $425M. Peer-median analysis yields $3.8B, derived from three Series C biotech peers with valuations ranging from $3.1B to $10.3B. The disparity reflects heterogeneity within early-stage biotech; Colossal's $10.3B valuation suggests outlier positioning, likely driven by differentiated technology or market narrative.\n\nTriangulation produces a range of $361M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The wide spread reflects tension between the conservative stage-progression methodology and the elevated peer cohort. Key uncertainties include peer selection robustness\u2014whether the three comparables fully represent Loyal's technology maturity and clinical-stage progression\u2014and whether Colossal represents a sustainable valuation benchmark or an outlier. Revenue or clinical-stage visibility would materially narrow this range.",
