      "narrative": "Viam is a Series C robotics and manufacturing software platform founded by Eliot Horowitz, having raised $117M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private robotics and manufacturing firms at Series B through Series D stages, supplemented by 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $199M. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014including Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Hadrian ($1.6B, Series D)\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B.\n\nThe combined analysis supports a valuation range of $169M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median implied value of $924M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and maturity variation within the peer set; Series B comparables sit materially higher than stage-progression mechanics would suggest, while the stage-based method assumes more conservative growth. Key uncertainties include Viam's revenue scale and growth rate relative to peers, customer concentration, and whether frontier-tech robotics software commands stage-adjusted premiums or discounts to comparable SaaS progression.",
