      "narrative": "ASI is a Series B space and aerospace company founded by Phillip Buckendorf, Kris Dorosz, and Lucas Kukielka. The company has raised $56.1M to date. Valuation analysis draws on two applicable methodologies against a universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers and 5 public Space & Aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $56.1M total raised proxy, implying a $107M valuation. Peer-median anchoring examines four same-sector peers\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring was not applicable, as ASI's revenue is not on file; the sector median P/S across 6 public comps stands at 24.6x.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $91M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $878M across both applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty: stage-progression methods anchor to capital raised and assume standardized advancement multiples, while peer-median approaches are sensitive to composition (one outlier peer at $8.0B materially widens the range). Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peers, and technology defensibility within the crowded space sector.",
