      "narrative": "Orbital Sidekick is a Series C-stage space & aerospace company founded by Tushar Prabhakar and Daniel Katz, having raised $47.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 7 private peers in the same sector and stage (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Impulse Space at $4.3B, Apex Space at $2.3B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, and Varda Space Industries at $1.6B), alongside 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trading at a median price-to-sales of 24.6x.\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $48M raised proxy as a base and applying a 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $81M. The peer-median method, based on seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies, yields $2.0B (range: $1.15B\u2013$8.0B). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures. The triangulation of these two methods produces a low-to-high range of $69M to $2.3B, with a median estimate of $1.0B.\n\nThe wide range reflects material uncertainty around stage-appropriate valuation levels in space & aerospace, where private comps span from early-stage to growth-stage valuations. The peer-median method carries greater weight given its sample size and sector specificity, though the stage-progression floor suggests downside protection if near-term capital constraints materialize.",
