      "narrative": "Burro is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $44.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine companies\u2014one publicly traded and eight private firms in the robotics sector at comparable or adjacent stages, including Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Hadrian.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy base ($45M) and applying a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C-to-next-stage progression, implies a valuation of $76M. Peer-median analysis across seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. The peer sample includes Exotec at $2.0B (Series D), Hadrian and Dexterity each at $1.6B (Series D and B respectively), and Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B (Series B).\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range: $65M on the low end (stage-progression), $863M at the median, and $1.9B at the high end (peer-ceiling). The stage-progression method likely underweights Burro's market position relative to funded peers, while the peer-median approach may not fully account for Burro's earlier stage positioning within Series C. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, unit economics, and competitive differentiation relative to the peer cohort, which would substantially narrow this range.",
