      "narrative": "Tutor Intelligence is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Alon Kosowsky-Sachs and Josh Gruenstein that has raised $42.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 5 private peers in the same sector and stage proximity, including Humanoid ($1.4B, Series A), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for post-money value, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implying a valuation of $85M. Peer-median methodology benchmarks against the five comparables listed above, which exhibit a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B, directly implying $1.6B for Tutor Intelligence.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a range of $72M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $868M. The wide dispersion reflects fundamental uncertainty regarding where Tutor Intelligence sits relative to its peer set\u2014whether it trades closer to early-stage Seed/Series A valuations or commands premium multiples reflective of later-stage momentum. Stage progression alone supports $85M; peer comparables suggest materially higher valuations. Resolution of this gap depends on company-specific traction, capital efficiency, and market position relative to named competitors.",
