      "narrative": "TerraDepth is a Series C-stage transportation company founded by Judson Kauffman and Josef Wolfel. The broader transportation tech sector includes eight identified private peers\u2014including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Slate Auto, and ZeroAvia\u2014though no public comparables exist. The narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier contains insufficient datapoints to support conventional multiples-based triangulation.\n\nStage-progression analysis, the applicable method here, uses TerraDepth's $31.1M total raised as a proxy for implied pre-money valuation, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C-to-subsequent-round progression. This approach yields an implied valuation of $53M. The 1.7x multiplier reflects observed market discipline in transportation venture financing over the relevant period, though this multiplier varies with market conditions and company-specific risk.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $45M to $61M, centered on $53M. This range reflects stage-appropriate progression from deployed capital but carries material uncertainty: the absence of same-stage comparable transactions in transportation prevents cross-check validation via peer multiples, and the method relies on aggregate stage-progression conventions rather than sector-specific benchmarks. Key sensitivities include management execution risk, capital efficiency relative to peer burn profiles, and timing to exit or follow-on capital events.",
