      "narrative": "Corvus Robotics is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $28.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 9 comparable companies (1 public, 8 private) operating in the same sector and stage, including Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Hadrian.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy baseline of $28M and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C progression, yields $48M. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. The peer set exhibits material dispersion, reflecting stage heterogeneity (Series B through Series D) and varying capital efficiency within robotics.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $41M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $849M. The wide spread reflects the tension between stage-progression methodology\u2014which anchors to early-stage capital deployed\u2014and peer-median methodology, which reflects current market valuations for more mature robotics companies. Key uncertainties include Corvus's position relative to peers on revenue and deployment scale, customer concentration, and whether recent robotics sector valuations have compressed since peer transactions closed.",
