      "narrative": "Beacon AI is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Matt Cox and Avinash Nair that has raised $26.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers in the Space & Aerospace sector, including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable to this stage and disclosure profile. Stage-progression analysis uses the $26.4M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $53M. Peer-median analysis references three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Cowboy Space at $2.0B (Series B), Aalyria at $1.3B (Series B), and Starcloud at $1.1B (Seed)\u2014producing a median of $1.3B. Public-comp anchoring is inapplicable due to absence of target revenue data, though the sector P/S median stands at 24.6x across the five public names. The Public-Comp Anchoring method would require revenue disclosure unavailable for this private company.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $45M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $676M across the two applicable methods. This wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around whether Beacon AI is more accurately characterized by its near-term fundraising trajectory or by the valuation clustering of mature, late-stage space-tech peers. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, technical differentiation, and pathway to cash flow generation relative to the peer set.",
