      "narrative": "CruxOCM is a Series A climate and energy technology company founded by Roger Shirt and Vicki Knott that has raised $26.1M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector comprises one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, no narrowly-filtered peer set of same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with sufficient data density exists to support peer-median valuation.\n\nStage-progression methodology is applicable and drives the primary valuation signal. Using total capital raised ($26.1M) as a value proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression yields an implied valuation of $52.2M. This method reflects the step-change in company maturity and risk profile between seed/early institutional funding and Series A scaling.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $44M to $60M, with a median of $52.2M. This range reflects the single triangulation method available and incorporates standard uncertainty bounds around stage-progression assumptions. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 2.0x multiplier for CruxOCM's specific risk profile relative to sector norms, revenue trajectory visibility, and competitive positioning within frontier climate tech. A refined estimate would require additional revenue, unit economics, or cohort-specific comparables data.",
