      "narrative": "Nuview is a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Clint and Katie Graumann that has raised $22.9M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, with particular focus on 3 same-sector adjacently-staged private comparables.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis uses the $23M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a typical 2.0x multiplier for Series A to post-Series A step-up, yielding $46M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector companies (Cowboy Space at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Starcloud at $1.1B) produces a $1.3B median with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 24.6x across the sector) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue. These two applicable methods triangulate to a range of $39M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $673M across the two approaches.\n\nThe wide spread reflects material stage and maturity dispersion within the peer set. Stage-progression implies a near-term valuation toward the lower bound, while peer-median reflects later-stage comparables. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, technology differentiation relative to peers, and capital intensity of the development path.",
