      "narrative": "Safire is a Series C climate and energy company founded by John Lee and Mike Grubbs, having raised $16.7M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), alongside one public comparable and a broader private frontier-tech universe of eight additional peers.\n\nTwo methods were applied to establish a valuation range. The stage-progression approach, using total capital raised as a baseline proxy, applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C to subsequent-stage transitions, implying a valuation of $28M. The peer-median method references the three direct comparables, which span $700M to $3.0B with a median of $1.0B, directly implying $1.0B. The wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014ranging from $700M to $3.0B\u2014reflects material heterogeneity within the climate and energy tech sector even at equivalent stages.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $24M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $514M. This wide range reflects fundamental uncertainty regarding Safire's competitive positioning and unit economics relative to the peer set. The stage-progression method likely understates value given the substantial capital efficiency demonstrated by peers at equivalent stages. Key uncertainties include Safire's technology maturity, path to commercialization, capital efficiency, and competitive differentiation within a rapidly evolving sector.",
