      "narrative": "Specter Aerospace, a Series C space and aerospace company founded by Felipe Gomez del Campo and Drew Weibel, has raised $14.4M to date. Valuation analysis applies two applicable methods against a comparable universe of 7 private peers in the same sector and stage, alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) for reference.\n\nStage-progression analysis anchors to the $14.4M total raised and applies a 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implying a valuation of $24M. Peer-median methodology draws on 7 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies\u2014including Sierra Space ($8.0B), Impulse Space ($4.3B), Apex Space ($2.3B), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), and Varda Space Industries ($1.6B)\u2014yielding a median of $2.0B with a range of $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring was not applied due to absence of target revenue data, though the sector median P/S multiple is 24.6x across public comparables.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $21M (low) to $2.3B (high) with a median of $1.0B. The wide dispersion reflects structural uncertainty: early-stage capitalization versus peer valuations dependent on technology maturity, commercial traction, and customer pipeline visibility. Resolution of these factors will materially narrow the range in subsequent rounds.",
