      "narrative": "Danti, a Seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Jesse Kallman and Martice Nicks III, has raised $10.9M to date. The broader Space & Aerospace sector comprises 14 private peers and 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), though the private peer set lacks sufficient granularity for direct median benchmarking at Danti's stage and scale.\n\nAnalysis relies on stage-progression methodology, applying a 2.5x multiplier to the $10.9M raised as a valuation proxy. This approach, standard for Seed-to-Series A transitions in venture markets, yields an implied valuation of $27M. Public comparables in Space & Aerospace trade at a median 24.6x revenue multiple, but without disclosed revenue figures for Danti, this anchor cannot be operationalized. The peer-median method is not applicable given insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage private comparables meeting minimum sample thresholds.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $23M to $31M, centered on $27M. Key uncertainties include: absence of revenue disclosure typical to private companies, limiting public-comp triangulation; thinness of private comparable data at the Seed stage within Space & Aerospace; and sensitivity to stage-step assumptions in a capital-intensive sector where funding rounds may not correlate predictably with value creation. Further due diligence on technology differentiation and customer validation would refine this range.",
