      "narrative": "Cognitive Space, a Seed-stage space & aerospace company founded by Guy de Carufel, has raised $10.3M to date. The valuation universe consists of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE, though narrow peer matching proved limited.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using $10.3M in total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A progression yields $26M. Peer-median analysis failed due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables in the Space & Aerospace sector\u2014while 14 peers exist in the sector, the narrow filters (same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier) returned fewer than the required three datapoints. Public-comp anchoring using the 6-ticker Space & Aerospace median P/S of 24.6x could not be applied because Cognitive Space's revenue is not disclosed, a common constraint with private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $22M to $30M, with a median point of $26M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the single applicable method. Key uncertainties include the absence of sufficiently tight private peer comparables at seed stage and lack of revenue disclosure, which prevents cross-check validation via public multiples. The valuation remains highly sensitive to near-term financing outcomes and revenue trajectory.",
