      "narrative": "Ephemeris Net is a Seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Dennis Fong and Nicolas Brown. The target has raised $3M to date. The broader Space & Aerospace sector includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and a deep roster of private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, Sierra Space, ICEYE, and Starcloud, though narrow peer matching at the Seed stage is constrained.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using $3M in total raised as a proxy for implied Seed valuation, a standard Seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $8M. Peer-median benchmarking was not viable; while 14 same-sector private companies exist, fewer than three matched narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or comparable valuation tier), making narrow-set medians unreliable. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales could not be applied, as target revenue is not on file\u2014standard for early-stage private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6M to $9M, centered at $8M, derived from a single method. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable Seed-stage transaction data in Space & Aerospace, lack of target revenue visibility, and the reliance on a generic stage-progression multiplier rather than sector-specific step-up calibration. Additional revenue or customer traction data would enable public-comp anchoring and strengthen the range.",
