      "narrative": "Airrow, a Defense & Security seed-stage company founded by Menachem Fehler and David Kaye, has raised $350K to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI, alongside public comparables DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the $350K total raised as a base proxy, applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implying a valuation of $875K. The Peer-Median method examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B Seed, Singularity at $400M Series A, and NODA AI at $125M Series A), establishing a median valuation of $400M with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a low of $744K, a median of $200M, and a high of $460M across these two methods. The wide dispersion reflects substantial uncertainty inherent in early-stage valuation, particularly the significant gap between stage-progression mechanics and peer multiples. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the peer set at the earliest stage, the applicability of late-stage comparable valuations to a nascent seed company, and the absence of revenue or traction metrics to anchor valuation. The median should be weighted cautiously given the limited methodological convergence.",
